1
00:00:01,313 --> 00:00:03,483
(Between Fantasy and Reality)

2
00:00:04,153 --> 00:00:05,853
Nice to see you, everyone.

3
00:00:06,393 --> 00:00:07,452
You two haven't met yet, right?

4
00:00:07,453 --> 00:00:09,122
- We haven't. It's nice to meet you. - It's nice to meet you. Hello.

5
00:00:09,123 --> 00:00:10,523
- My gosh. - Hello.

6
00:00:10,793 --> 00:00:12,333
Have you watched some of his clips?

7
00:00:12,463 --> 00:00:14,962
- They were quite bold. - Right.

8
00:00:14,963 --> 00:00:16,562
And he gives off this vibe...

9
00:00:16,563 --> 00:00:18,162
- of a man living in nature. - Yes.

10
00:00:18,163 --> 00:00:19,673
That's putting it nicely.

11
00:00:19,773 --> 00:00:20,932
You know, she's a sweet girl.

12
00:00:20,933 --> 00:00:23,103
But he doesn't give off that vibe...

13
00:00:23,503 --> 00:00:25,042
- in the studio. - Yes.

14
00:00:25,043 --> 00:00:26,313
- Does he look normal enough? - Right.

15
00:00:26,513 --> 00:00:27,513
(A normal smile)

16
00:00:27,514 --> 00:00:28,572
"He looks normal."

17
00:00:28,573 --> 00:00:29,582
- Is that what you mean? - He looks normal and all.

18
00:00:29,583 --> 00:00:31,512
That's a lengthy way of saying he looks surprisingly normal.

19
00:00:31,513 --> 00:00:33,083
(That's a lengthy way of saying he looks surprisingly normal.)

20
00:00:33,783 --> 00:00:36,023
(Beware of Fantasy)

21
00:00:37,553 --> 00:00:38,553
(Chirping)

22
00:00:38,953 --> 00:00:39,953
(Chirping)

23
00:00:40,953 --> 00:00:42,493
(As the chirping sound of the birds becomes his lullaby,)

24
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:45,063
(Dae Ho is enjoying his restful day.)

25
00:00:45,993 --> 00:00:47,962
Yes. This is what I'm dreaming of.

26
00:00:47,963 --> 00:00:49,632
That's such a happy moment.

27
00:00:49,633 --> 00:00:51,462
Lying down there in my work pants. Yes, that's it.

28
00:00:51,463 --> 00:00:53,033
This makes living in Seoul feel different.

29
00:00:53,233 --> 00:00:54,632
- You can hear the birds... - Right.

30
00:00:54,633 --> 00:00:55,742
- and the bugs... - Yes.

31
00:00:55,743 --> 00:00:56,842
when you live in a single-family house.

32
00:00:56,843 --> 00:00:57,973
I'm so envious of this.

33
00:01:00,043 --> 00:01:01,673
(Getting up)

34
00:01:04,413 --> 00:01:07,153
(Dae Ho walks out on top of the rooftop.)

35
00:01:11,683 --> 00:01:12,892
What a mess.

36
00:01:12,893 --> 00:01:16,063
(What a mess.)

37
00:01:18,863 --> 00:01:19,932
What is that?

38
00:01:19,933 --> 00:01:23,763
(The greenery is thick enough to cover the sky.)

39
00:01:24,833 --> 00:01:28,873
(It's surrounded by overgrown grass.)

40
00:01:30,043 --> 00:01:31,402
(Dae Ho's house has become a jungle.)

41
00:01:31,403 --> 00:01:32,473
That's me.

42
00:01:33,173 --> 00:01:34,872
(Even the wild animals can live safely in a place like this.)

43
00:01:34,873 --> 00:01:37,042
(Munching)

44
00:01:37,043 --> 00:01:38,812
CODE KUNST, you can go there and climb a tree.

45
00:01:38,813 --> 00:01:39,913
That was tasty.

46
00:01:41,753 --> 00:01:42,823
My gosh.

47
00:01:43,153 --> 00:01:44,623
I've been busy this year.

48
00:01:44,983 --> 00:01:47,053
On top of that, it rained a lot.

49
00:01:47,393 --> 00:01:49,293
- I haven't seen this much rain. - Me neither.

50
00:01:49,893 --> 00:01:51,923
When the rainy season was nearing,

51
00:01:52,093 --> 00:01:53,363
I took a look at my house.

52
00:01:53,533 --> 00:01:55,963
The house I used to remember is gone now.

53
00:01:57,303 --> 00:02:00,133
(Dae Ho's cozy fun space...)

54
00:02:00,373 --> 00:02:03,202
The grass was overgrown everywhere like a tropical rain forest.

55
00:02:03,203 --> 00:02:04,373
Even I was surprised.

56
00:02:05,443 --> 00:02:07,373
What? How many days has it been since you last took care of it?

57
00:02:07,643 --> 00:02:09,482
It's only been two weeks.

58
00:02:09,483 --> 00:02:10,682
It's the mountain.

59
00:02:10,683 --> 00:02:12,082
- It's near a mountain. - That's why it grows faster.

60
00:02:12,083 --> 00:02:13,553
- That happened in two weeks? - Yes.

61
00:02:13,713 --> 00:02:15,112
You need to pull it out, though.

62
00:02:15,113 --> 00:02:16,622
If I don't, it could damage the house.

63
00:02:16,623 --> 00:02:17,722
- Right. It could damage the house. - I...

64
00:02:17,723 --> 00:02:19,422
- But you... - Can it cover up the house?

65
00:02:19,423 --> 00:02:20,792
- Right. That's because... - Yes.

66
00:02:20,793 --> 00:02:22,792
- Roots could damage the house. - Yes.

67
00:02:22,793 --> 00:02:24,322
- The roots penetrate into the gaps. - They can pierce through the walls.

68
00:02:24,323 --> 00:02:25,362
- They can separate concrete walls. - My gosh.

69
00:02:25,363 --> 00:02:27,233
Plants can be really strong.

70
00:02:27,333 --> 00:02:28,533
(Fascinated)

71
00:02:29,433 --> 00:02:30,633
This is a mess.

72
00:02:31,063 --> 00:02:33,433
You have two houses, but you're usually on the rooftop.

73
00:02:35,773 --> 00:02:38,443
(He comes down from the rooftop and enters House 1.)

74
00:02:39,743 --> 00:02:40,773
Nana.

75
00:02:42,173 --> 00:02:44,143
Nana, my legs are killing me. Gosh.

76
00:02:44,483 --> 00:02:45,483
Nana.

77
00:02:45,483 --> 00:02:46,483
(What am I going to do with the tropical rain forest?)

78
00:02:46,484 --> 00:02:47,683
- My legs are killing me. - So cute.

79
00:02:47,883 --> 00:02:49,923
- Nana. - It's been a while, Nana.

80
00:02:50,223 --> 00:02:51,723
So he's practically a wild cat.

81
00:02:52,893 --> 00:02:54,453
He's living the life of a cheetah...

82
00:02:54,723 --> 00:02:55,993
- in the Serengeti. - Like a wild animal.

83
00:02:57,293 --> 00:02:58,592
(I like the wilderness that is my home.)

84
00:02:58,593 --> 00:03:00,493
Nana, I'll be back.

85
00:03:01,593 --> 00:03:03,663
(He says bye to Nana who's living in the wild.)

86
00:03:05,203 --> 00:03:09,343
(He goes out with a backpack on.)

87
00:03:09,843 --> 00:03:12,043
You're going out in those pants.

88
00:03:12,643 --> 00:03:14,713
- At least he's wearing pants. - Right.

89
00:03:15,343 --> 00:03:16,383
That's right.

90
00:03:16,543 --> 00:03:18,542
I actually thought, "He bought new pants."

91
00:03:18,543 --> 00:03:19,913
- I had the same thought. - Right.

92
00:03:20,213 --> 00:03:22,212
- That's right. - The floral pants are new.

93
00:03:22,213 --> 00:03:23,752
- "I haven't seen those pants." - I haven't seen them before.

94
00:03:23,753 --> 00:03:25,052
That crossed my mind.

95
00:03:25,053 --> 00:03:27,153
(Dae Ho is finally out of his winter clothes.)

96
00:03:27,253 --> 00:03:28,393
- I spent a fortune on them. - My gosh.

97
00:03:28,593 --> 00:03:30,123
A fortune?

98
00:03:30,863 --> 00:03:33,593
(Dae Ho is wearing an expensive outfit outside.)

99
00:03:34,463 --> 00:03:36,163
(Sighing)

100
00:03:37,603 --> 00:03:39,673
(He stops walking only after taking a few steps.)

101
00:03:39,773 --> 00:03:40,833
What is it?

102
00:03:43,173 --> 00:03:44,243
- What happened? - What?

103
00:03:44,403 --> 00:03:46,173
- Did Damarghini run into the house? - What a mess.

104
00:03:46,413 --> 00:03:47,513
No. It didn't.

105
00:03:48,043 --> 00:03:49,482
- My gosh. - What happened?

106
00:03:49,483 --> 00:03:51,682
- Seriously. It looks doomed. - Wait. This is...

107
00:03:51,683 --> 00:03:53,913
- Right. - Yes, this is like "I Am Legend."

108
00:03:54,283 --> 00:03:55,383
- Gosh. - Or "Mars on Earth."

109
00:03:55,583 --> 00:03:57,022
It's that fertile?

110
00:03:57,023 --> 00:03:58,323
(Horrified)

111
00:03:58,993 --> 00:04:00,922
(Daunting)

112
00:04:00,923 --> 00:04:03,392
- It's that tree. That especially... - That tree is the worst.

113
00:04:03,393 --> 00:04:05,322
- That's the problem. Yes. - That's the problem.

114
00:04:05,323 --> 00:04:06,862
- That's the crazy one. - Seriously.

115
00:04:06,863 --> 00:04:08,192
- You must pull it when you see it. - Right.

116
00:04:08,193 --> 00:04:09,332
That's scary.

117
00:04:09,333 --> 00:04:11,433
- Its life force is amazing. - It's crazy.

118
00:04:12,373 --> 00:04:13,803
Gosh, that's a mess too.

119
00:04:14,703 --> 00:04:16,303
I'm sorry. My gosh.

120
00:04:17,703 --> 00:04:18,903
It rained way too much this year.

121
00:04:18,973 --> 00:04:23,243
Vivarium enthusiasts say, "It's grown rampant."

122
00:04:23,383 --> 00:04:24,383
There's a time...

123
00:04:24,384 --> 00:04:25,442
- it hits a crazy growth period. - Right.

124
00:04:25,443 --> 00:04:26,552
- It's like an explosion. - It happens out of the blue.

125
00:04:26,553 --> 00:04:29,223
The vines that swallowed my car...

126
00:04:29,683 --> 00:04:30,822
weren't there before.

127
00:04:30,823 --> 00:04:31,952
It only took two weeks.

128
00:04:31,953 --> 00:04:35,823
Within two weeks, they covered up the window shield of my car.

129
00:04:37,023 --> 00:04:38,622
Where can you even start?

130
00:04:38,623 --> 00:04:39,862
- Gosh. - I'd be so lost.

131
00:04:39,863 --> 00:04:41,293
- Seriously. - I'm worried the car broke down.

132
00:04:42,063 --> 00:04:44,963
(I don't know what to do, but I must save Damarghini.)

133
00:04:45,973 --> 00:04:48,672
I needed to use scissors to remove them.

134
00:04:48,673 --> 00:04:50,102
- Even a sickle is useless here. - I see.

135
00:04:50,103 --> 00:04:51,372
- You must pull them by hand. - They're so tough.

136
00:04:51,373 --> 00:04:52,473
- Really? - Yes.

137
00:04:52,843 --> 00:04:54,973
- Pull them by hand. - They all cling onto each other.

138
00:04:55,273 --> 00:04:57,313
- They're like never-ending vines. - Yes.

139
00:04:58,383 --> 00:05:00,883
(He starts playing a tug of war with the vines.)

140
00:05:02,783 --> 00:05:04,483
Gosh, what happened here?

141
00:05:05,453 --> 00:05:06,593
Why is that coming out of my truck?

142
00:05:08,693 --> 00:05:09,892
- It got inside. - This...

143
00:05:09,893 --> 00:05:11,792
- Gosh, that's crazy. - Goodness.

144
00:05:11,793 --> 00:05:13,533
I can't even tell how much of my car is covered in vines.

145
00:05:13,863 --> 00:05:15,233
Why did this grow inside my car?

146
00:05:15,493 --> 00:05:16,663
- I bet it's everywhere. - My gosh.

147
00:05:17,703 --> 00:05:19,703
(Getting the creeps)

148
00:05:20,403 --> 00:05:22,103
How did it get inside here? Wait.

149
00:05:22,333 --> 00:05:23,372
Oh, no.

150
00:05:23,373 --> 00:05:25,672
The thing is that, it went inside the wheel.

151
00:05:25,673 --> 00:05:26,943
Even if I tried to pull it out,

152
00:05:27,113 --> 00:05:28,472
I couldn't tell how deep the root was.

153
00:05:28,473 --> 00:05:29,512
- That's crazy. - It kept coming out.

154
00:05:29,513 --> 00:05:32,342
I still don't know. I removed everything visible to my eye,

155
00:05:32,343 --> 00:05:34,913
but there could still be more vines, wrapping around parts of my car.

156
00:05:35,013 --> 00:05:36,082
I was shocked.

157
00:05:36,083 --> 00:05:38,323
Gosh, it got all the way inside my car.

158
00:05:38,923 --> 00:05:41,322
- But aren't they really prickly? - They're so prickly.

159
00:05:41,323 --> 00:05:42,962
Right. I remember them being very prickly.

160
00:05:42,963 --> 00:05:44,193
Gosh, that's prickly.

161
00:05:48,593 --> 00:05:49,702
Darn.

162
00:05:49,703 --> 00:05:52,003
(He overcomes the prickly bushes and keeps working at it.)

163
00:05:54,003 --> 00:05:55,203
(Losing his balance)

164
00:05:55,403 --> 00:05:56,742
- Gosh. - They coiled around my house.

165
00:05:56,743 --> 00:05:59,943
(The battle against the vines doesn't seem to end.)

166
00:06:01,273 --> 00:06:03,043
(Sticking on his shirt)

167
00:06:03,943 --> 00:06:06,313
I thought the leaves were a part of the original design.

168
00:06:08,013 --> 00:06:10,653
(With the unexpected presents on his T-shirt,)

169
00:06:11,523 --> 00:06:15,092
(he successfully rescues Damarghini.)

170
00:06:15,093 --> 00:06:16,163
Okay.

171
00:06:16,463 --> 00:06:18,563
(He gets into Damarghini right after the clean-up.)

172
00:06:19,833 --> 00:06:21,963
(His heart is pounding for some reason.)

173
00:06:22,503 --> 00:06:23,562
Let's go, Dama.

174
00:06:23,563 --> 00:06:26,473
- It's still operating. - It's still working really well.

175
00:06:27,733 --> 00:06:28,772
(He sets out to soothe Damarghini for what it has to put up with.)

176
00:06:28,773 --> 00:06:30,503
Let's go.

177
00:06:32,043 --> 00:06:34,412
- I got a vehicle inspection. - Yes.

178
00:06:34,413 --> 00:06:36,283
- It's in perfect condition. - It's operating well.

179
00:06:36,543 --> 00:06:38,213
- I was told to give it more oil. - Yes.

180
00:06:38,813 --> 00:06:40,153
Gosh, this is the place.

181
00:06:41,583 --> 00:06:42,652
(He arrives at his destination.)

182
00:06:42,653 --> 00:06:44,123
Okay.

183
00:06:45,423 --> 00:06:47,693
- You left in those stretchy pants. - This is the place. Okay.

184
00:06:47,853 --> 00:06:49,522
He went to the downtown area in those stretchy pants.

185
00:06:49,523 --> 00:06:52,123
(Impressed)

186
00:06:53,163 --> 00:06:54,662
(He arrives at a self-service car wash in his unusual outfit.)

187
00:06:54,663 --> 00:06:56,002
He went to wash his car.

188
00:06:56,003 --> 00:06:58,402
I've done that about 100 times.

189
00:06:58,403 --> 00:06:59,572
Really?

190
00:06:59,573 --> 00:07:00,673
That's fun.

191
00:07:01,703 --> 00:07:03,973
Right now, Damarghini...

192
00:07:04,103 --> 00:07:07,773
has been with me for five years. It's been that long.

193
00:07:08,373 --> 00:07:10,583
I've been busy. So unlike before,

194
00:07:10,683 --> 00:07:13,253
I felt that I haven't done much to take care of it.

195
00:07:13,513 --> 00:07:17,553
(Damarghini, we used to be so happy together.)

196
00:07:18,153 --> 00:07:21,393
It's been out in the rain and snow so many times.

197
00:07:21,553 --> 00:07:23,822
The exterior of my car seemed very dusty.

198
00:07:23,823 --> 00:07:26,333
So Damarghini must be itchy all over.

199
00:07:26,563 --> 00:07:27,963
I wanted to give it a bath.

200
00:07:28,163 --> 00:07:29,932
- That's why I went there. - I've never seen anyone...

201
00:07:29,933 --> 00:07:31,703
so attached to their car...

202
00:07:32,063 --> 00:07:33,532
since the cartoon, "Bumpety Boo."

203
00:07:33,533 --> 00:07:36,573
To tell you the truth, I had never washed...

204
00:07:36,943 --> 00:07:38,903
Damarghini before. Not even once.

205
00:07:39,073 --> 00:07:40,113
Really?

206
00:07:40,513 --> 00:07:41,742
Once it rained,

207
00:07:41,743 --> 00:07:42,942
- that counted as a car wash. - Sure.

208
00:07:42,943 --> 00:07:44,042
You saved five years' worth...

209
00:07:44,043 --> 00:07:45,143
- of car wash fees. - Right.

210
00:07:45,743 --> 00:07:47,253
It's been out in the rain so much.

211
00:07:47,453 --> 00:07:51,253
So the seats were covered in mold.

212
00:07:51,983 --> 00:07:54,593
(A thick layer of old dust and dirt)

213
00:07:55,193 --> 00:07:57,662
- Gosh, you never cleaned it. - It was still there.

214
00:07:57,663 --> 00:07:59,393
(Mold has taken over the car.)

215
00:07:59,563 --> 00:08:00,733
- Gosh. - Oh, no.

216
00:08:00,993 --> 00:08:02,493
I never want to ride his truck again.

217
00:08:03,433 --> 00:08:04,802
It was a terrifying memory.

218
00:08:04,803 --> 00:08:05,803
(Trembling in fear)

219
00:08:06,603 --> 00:08:08,773
I thought about getting the automatic car wash.

220
00:08:09,503 --> 00:08:11,273
But I have a rack on the roof of my truck.

221
00:08:11,473 --> 00:08:14,012
Because of the height, automatic car washes weren't...

222
00:08:14,013 --> 00:08:15,242
- Right. You must remove that first. - an option.

223
00:08:15,243 --> 00:08:16,483
What a great excuse.

224
00:08:17,013 --> 00:08:18,683
I had never been there before.

225
00:08:18,883 --> 00:08:21,283
I didn't know where to start or how to go about this.

226
00:08:21,453 --> 00:08:24,583
I was excited and nervous at the same time.

227
00:08:25,553 --> 00:08:27,793
That's how I felt. I was scared too.

228
00:08:29,493 --> 00:08:30,623
How do I do this?

229
00:08:32,893 --> 00:08:35,192
I was new to it. So I was completely lost.

230
00:08:35,193 --> 00:08:36,503
(The newbie is lost from the beginning.)

231
00:08:36,833 --> 00:08:38,763
(Dazed)

232
00:08:39,703 --> 00:08:42,572
(Clicking)

233
00:08:42,573 --> 00:08:43,803
You should put in the money first.

234
00:08:44,273 --> 00:08:46,772
- I see. I must put in money. - I thought I could just start.

235
00:08:46,773 --> 00:08:48,173
I thought I had to pay at the end.

236
00:08:50,583 --> 00:08:52,583
Right. Nothing is free in life.

237
00:08:54,013 --> 00:08:55,883
(He tries to pay for it with his phone.)

238
00:08:57,753 --> 00:08:59,992
(Quiet)

239
00:08:59,993 --> 00:09:01,253
What? Why isn't it working?

240
00:09:02,293 --> 00:09:03,822
Did you try to pay with your transportation card?

241
00:09:03,823 --> 00:09:06,792
- No. With my phone. - Is that the T-money card?

242
00:09:06,793 --> 00:09:07,992
(Tapping)

243
00:09:07,993 --> 00:09:10,863
(No matter how many times he puts it there, it doesn't work.)

244
00:09:11,863 --> 00:09:13,503
You'll have to insert their card.

245
00:09:13,973 --> 00:09:15,672
I don't think they accept credit cards.

246
00:09:15,673 --> 00:09:17,473
There are special cards just for the car washes.

247
00:09:17,703 --> 00:09:18,842
(Pressing on it)

248
00:09:18,843 --> 00:09:20,413
Hold on. Why...

249
00:09:20,513 --> 00:09:22,683
(Is this out of order?)

250
00:09:22,883 --> 00:09:24,013
Why isn't it working?

251
00:09:24,483 --> 00:09:26,553
- That's... - You just have to read the signs.

252
00:09:26,853 --> 00:09:28,183
You just have to read the signs.

253
00:09:28,283 --> 00:09:29,353
Right.

254
00:09:30,053 --> 00:09:31,682
(It's all over the car wash.)

255
00:09:31,683 --> 00:09:32,752
There it is.

256
00:09:32,753 --> 00:09:34,793
- It said to get a card there. - That's the instruction.

257
00:09:34,893 --> 00:09:36,222
Come on, man. You have to buy the card first.

258
00:09:36,223 --> 00:09:37,523
The card for the car washes.

259
00:09:38,093 --> 00:09:39,733
It says, "Please."

260
00:09:40,033 --> 00:09:42,432
When I was there, I was completely clueless.

261
00:09:42,433 --> 00:09:44,432
Those words failed me.

262
00:09:44,433 --> 00:09:46,032
- I was flustered. - Really?

263
00:09:46,033 --> 00:09:47,772
- But I know how that feels. - Right.

264
00:09:47,773 --> 00:09:49,902
When I went to a self-service gas station for the first time,

265
00:09:49,903 --> 00:09:51,673
there was an overwhelming vibe.

266
00:09:52,003 --> 00:09:53,842
- I didn't want to mess it up. - She has everyone's back.

267
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:55,343
- She does. - That's right.

268
00:09:55,443 --> 00:09:57,382
- She's so kind. - That's what I wanted to say.

269
00:09:57,383 --> 00:09:58,512
- That's... - Didn't you feel overwhelmed?

270
00:09:58,513 --> 00:10:00,183
- I did. - In case you pressed the wrong one.

271
00:10:02,783 --> 00:10:04,623
Wait. I can't pay it with my phone?

272
00:10:05,483 --> 00:10:06,553
Is he in there?

273
00:10:06,823 --> 00:10:08,053
Excuse me.

274
00:10:08,423 --> 00:10:09,563
- Hello. - Yes.

275
00:10:10,223 --> 00:10:12,162
You can top up the card with the amount you want.

276
00:10:12,163 --> 00:10:14,233
- You can tap the card on it. - I see.

277
00:10:15,393 --> 00:10:16,662
That's 21 dollars.

278
00:10:16,663 --> 00:10:17,802
- Okay. - The card costs a dollar.

279
00:10:17,803 --> 00:10:18,933
- Thank you. - Sure.

280
00:10:20,233 --> 00:10:21,332
- It worked. - It worked.

281
00:10:21,333 --> 00:10:22,333
(He manages to pay at last.)

282
00:10:23,043 --> 00:10:24,072
(The timer begins as soon as the payment goes through.)

283
00:10:24,073 --> 00:10:26,173
The time limit makes you nervous.

284
00:10:26,543 --> 00:10:27,972
(Staring)

285
00:10:27,973 --> 00:10:29,113
What? Did it start?

286
00:10:31,183 --> 00:10:32,312
I'm not ready yet.

287
00:10:32,313 --> 00:10:33,583
(Rummaging through)

288
00:10:35,153 --> 00:10:37,253
(He brought rubber gloves from his home.)

289
00:10:37,653 --> 00:10:38,882
(He gets fully ready for his first car wash.)

290
00:10:38,883 --> 00:10:41,093
Gosh, he already wasted the first cycle.

291
00:10:42,223 --> 00:10:44,593
(Slow)

292
00:10:44,663 --> 00:10:45,692
Darn.

293
00:10:45,693 --> 00:10:46,733
My gosh.

294
00:10:46,833 --> 00:10:48,362
I didn't know it'd start right away.

295
00:10:48,363 --> 00:10:49,902
- But... - You thought you had to use water.

296
00:10:49,903 --> 00:10:51,003
- Exactly. - I see.

297
00:10:51,103 --> 00:10:53,173
- Oh, no. - But the timer started right away.

298
00:10:53,673 --> 00:10:55,803
(He's taking his sweet time without looking at the timer.)

299
00:10:56,443 --> 00:10:57,543
Why isn't it working?

300
00:10:57,743 --> 00:10:58,903
Press it now.

301
00:11:00,743 --> 00:11:01,813
Do I press this?

302
00:11:02,843 --> 00:11:03,943
My gosh.

303
00:11:04,213 --> 00:11:05,882
(He finally begins and has wasted 1 minute and 10 seconds.)

304
00:11:05,883 --> 00:11:07,513
- Gosh, that's scary. - My gosh.

305
00:11:07,713 --> 00:11:08,813
- The water came out right away. - My gosh.

306
00:11:10,353 --> 00:11:12,223
(Surprised)

307
00:11:12,453 --> 00:11:14,093
The water came out strong.

308
00:11:14,293 --> 00:11:15,422
That feels great.

309
00:11:15,423 --> 00:11:17,222
- Gosh, this looks like a game. - This hits the spot.

310
00:11:17,223 --> 00:11:19,633
(This hits the spot.)

311
00:11:20,293 --> 00:11:21,762
- The water pressure is good there. - That must feel good.

312
00:11:21,763 --> 00:11:23,363
- It felt great. - It felt so good.

313
00:11:23,663 --> 00:11:25,002
That must hit the spot.

314
00:11:25,003 --> 00:11:26,233
(It's time to wash off the dirt and make it look spotless.)

315
00:11:26,403 --> 00:11:28,903
I should've come here a long time ago. This is so convenient.

316
00:11:29,333 --> 00:11:30,443
Gosh, this is amazing.

317
00:11:30,903 --> 00:11:32,043
My gosh, that hits the spot.

318
00:11:32,303 --> 00:11:33,973
(Thoroughly enjoying)

319
00:11:35,413 --> 00:11:36,413
(Stopping)

320
00:11:36,414 --> 00:11:37,543
What?

321
00:11:38,613 --> 00:11:39,882
- Oh, no. - What?

322
00:11:39,883 --> 00:11:40,983
Your time is up.

323
00:11:41,253 --> 00:11:43,283
- You took your sweet time. - What?

324
00:11:44,323 --> 00:11:45,453
I have to pay again?

325
00:11:47,023 --> 00:11:48,523
- Gosh. Oh, no. - My goodness.

326
00:11:49,193 --> 00:11:50,663
I must hurry up.

327
00:11:52,993 --> 00:11:54,492
Gosh, that hits the spot.

328
00:11:54,493 --> 00:11:55,993
(Washing every nook and cranny of his car thoroughly)

329
00:11:56,103 --> 00:11:57,633
Why did you do that? There's a system that cleans the bottom.

330
00:11:58,533 --> 00:12:00,303
- They didn't have it there. - It's not working.

331
00:12:01,103 --> 00:12:02,672
Four, three, two...

332
00:12:02,673 --> 00:12:04,643
- Yes, they have it. - They got it. There it is.

333
00:12:05,803 --> 00:12:07,672
- The sign... - It says so on the board.

334
00:12:07,673 --> 00:12:09,913
Learn how to read Korean, not how to wash cars.

335
00:12:12,113 --> 00:12:13,613
When did your brain start betraying you?

336
00:12:15,283 --> 00:12:17,583
It must've stopped working when he cried that day.

337
00:12:18,383 --> 00:12:20,052
When Kian84 cried? That was...

338
00:12:20,053 --> 00:12:21,153
Darn it.

339
00:12:21,893 --> 00:12:24,163
(Tears, the friendship formula of men born in 1984)

340
00:12:24,963 --> 00:12:26,693
Four, three, two...

341
00:12:27,093 --> 00:12:28,162
- What? - Gosh.

342
00:12:28,163 --> 00:12:29,362
- I know. I like that. - Wait.

343
00:12:29,363 --> 00:12:30,932
I only had two seconds left.

344
00:12:30,933 --> 00:12:32,502
- It was a waste. - You should use them up.

345
00:12:32,503 --> 00:12:34,702
- Like the last minute at karaoke. - Right.

346
00:12:34,703 --> 00:12:36,603
It's like the song, "100 Great People Who Made Korea Shine."

347
00:12:36,743 --> 00:12:37,873
Is this it?

348
00:12:38,603 --> 00:12:39,912
That's it.

349
00:12:39,913 --> 00:12:42,573
(He sprays the detergent foam.)

350
00:12:43,213 --> 00:12:44,413
That step feels good.

351
00:12:45,283 --> 00:12:46,782
- Gosh, this is fun. - That was fun.

352
00:12:46,783 --> 00:12:48,282
That ought to feel good.

353
00:12:48,283 --> 00:12:49,753
(White snow falls on top of Damarghini.)

354
00:12:52,353 --> 00:12:53,522
This is fun.

355
00:12:53,523 --> 00:12:54,723
(Chuckling)

356
00:12:56,223 --> 00:12:58,023
What? Darn.

357
00:12:58,293 --> 00:12:59,532
(He's not even halfway through with the detergent.)

358
00:12:59,533 --> 00:13:00,793
The cycles were too short.

359
00:13:01,963 --> 00:13:03,703
(He pays again.)

360
00:13:05,563 --> 00:13:06,703
This feels cool.

361
00:13:07,803 --> 00:13:08,902
What?

362
00:13:08,903 --> 00:13:11,142
Gosh, he couldn't finish spraying in the back.

363
00:13:11,143 --> 00:13:12,243
This is...

364
00:13:13,543 --> 00:13:14,673
What? Again?

365
00:13:15,243 --> 00:13:16,713
Will you spend 300 dollars there?

366
00:13:17,413 --> 00:13:18,743
- Did you spend all of it? - "Insufficient fund?"

367
00:13:19,583 --> 00:13:20,782
(In no time, he blows through 20 dollars.)

368
00:13:20,783 --> 00:13:23,082
You already spent 20 dollars there?

369
00:13:23,083 --> 00:13:25,083
- Just get a regular car wash. - No way.

370
00:13:25,223 --> 00:13:26,422
A regular car wash might be better.

371
00:13:26,423 --> 00:13:29,393
Given that this is his 1st time, 20 dollars is a modest amount.

372
00:13:29,563 --> 00:13:30,762
- Really? - Most newbies usually spend...

373
00:13:30,763 --> 00:13:31,922
- a lot more money than... - Right.

374
00:13:31,923 --> 00:13:33,663
they would for regular car washes.

375
00:13:33,993 --> 00:13:35,632
I've watched other people who were good at this.

376
00:13:35,633 --> 00:13:37,033
I've seen Gaeko do it.

377
00:13:37,163 --> 00:13:39,003
He just sprayed it a few times.

378
00:13:39,063 --> 00:13:41,303
He could do it within two minutes and still have time left.

379
00:13:41,533 --> 00:13:42,833
That's enough time.

380
00:13:42,943 --> 00:13:45,302
You kept spraying at the same spots.

381
00:13:45,303 --> 00:13:47,372
- Right. - You need to learn some tips.

382
00:13:47,373 --> 00:13:48,612
He didn't know.

383
00:13:48,613 --> 00:13:50,083
- Sir. - Yes.

384
00:13:50,213 --> 00:13:52,312
- Could you top up 20 more dollars? - You need more money, right?

385
00:13:52,313 --> 00:13:53,652
- I ran out. - Right.

386
00:13:53,653 --> 00:13:55,813
I was watching you. It looked like it was inevitable.

387
00:13:56,783 --> 00:13:57,823
Top up 20 dollars, please.

388
00:13:57,983 --> 00:13:59,052
- Twenty dollars? - Yes.

389
00:13:59,053 --> 00:14:00,192
(Total expense: 40 dollars)

390
00:14:00,193 --> 00:14:01,292
- Forty dollars? - Thank you.

391
00:14:01,293 --> 00:14:02,823
- That's the fee for a regular one. - Okay.

392
00:14:03,793 --> 00:14:04,993
I must start over.

393
00:14:06,263 --> 00:14:07,493
- You're doing it again? - You're spraying detergent again?

394
00:14:07,733 --> 00:14:10,003
- You can stop doing that. - That's enough!

395
00:14:10,503 --> 00:14:11,562
- That's... - It should be all white.

396
00:14:11,563 --> 00:14:13,003
Are you trying to bleach your car?

397
00:14:13,203 --> 00:14:16,543
I sprayed a lot of detergent because I can't trust myself.

398
00:14:17,003 --> 00:14:19,842
It felt like it would be clean if my truck completely turned white.

399
00:14:19,843 --> 00:14:21,612
I can understand that. I feel the same way.

400
00:14:21,613 --> 00:14:23,143
- Let's see how long you can do it. - Do you mean that?

401
00:14:23,713 --> 00:14:25,043
- Do you mean that, Joy? - That's...

402
00:14:25,213 --> 00:14:27,652
Yes. Seeing it covered in foam will put you at ease, right?

403
00:14:27,653 --> 00:14:29,653
- Right. - I'd feel the same way.

404
00:14:30,083 --> 00:14:32,352
(Mother Joresa is quite understanding.)

405
00:14:32,353 --> 00:14:35,153
Okay. Gosh, I didn't know the trick.

406
00:14:36,793 --> 00:14:37,993
- Okay. - It looks beautiful.

407
00:14:38,123 --> 00:14:39,162
It does.

408
00:14:39,163 --> 00:14:40,632
- It's like you painted it white. - Yes.

409
00:14:40,633 --> 00:14:42,363
It must look as white as that to reassure me.

410
00:14:43,003 --> 00:14:44,703
(He grabs something.)

411
00:14:45,163 --> 00:14:46,432
This isn't easy.

412
00:14:46,433 --> 00:14:47,473
(He removes the caked dirt himself.)

413
00:14:48,173 --> 00:14:49,572
Isn't that a loofah sponge?

414
00:14:49,573 --> 00:14:50,942
Can he use a loofah sponge?

415
00:14:50,943 --> 00:14:52,702
People use soft sponges on cars.

416
00:14:52,703 --> 00:14:53,712
I didn't know. I thought...

417
00:14:53,713 --> 00:14:55,412
- Soft ones. - I could use any sponge.

418
00:14:55,413 --> 00:14:56,943
Why didn't you use a stainless steel sponge then?

419
00:14:57,243 --> 00:14:58,813
- I'm not that dense. - Gosh.

420
00:15:00,483 --> 00:15:01,553
Doesn't it feel great?

421
00:15:03,323 --> 00:15:05,653
(I'm sorry for neglecting you all these years.)

422
00:15:06,053 --> 00:15:07,222
That must feel clean.

423
00:15:07,223 --> 00:15:09,223
(Let's meet again, fresh and renewed.)

424
00:15:09,893 --> 00:15:10,993
Doesn't it feel great?

425
00:15:14,233 --> 00:15:15,693
Gosh, it's dripping with dirty water.

426
00:15:17,263 --> 00:15:18,263
What?

427
00:15:19,103 --> 00:15:20,803
Oh, my. Look at this, dripping with dirty water.

428
00:15:21,503 --> 00:15:23,243
- Look. The water is black. - Gosh.

429
00:15:23,403 --> 00:15:24,673
It's that dirty?

430
00:15:25,371 --> 00:15:26,841
Gosh, it's dripping with dirty water.

431
00:15:28,411 --> 00:15:29,441
What?

432
00:15:30,281 --> 00:15:31,981
Oh, my. Look at this, dripping with dirty water.

433
00:15:32,681 --> 00:15:34,481
- Look. The water is black. - Gosh.

434
00:15:34,611 --> 00:15:35,780
It's that dirty?

435
00:15:35,781 --> 00:15:38,720
(The Rainbow Club members are speechless.)

436
00:15:38,721 --> 00:15:40,321
Joy, don't you have something to tell me?

437
00:15:41,691 --> 00:15:43,321
- Joy is slowly giving up. - Yes.

438
00:15:43,491 --> 00:15:44,560
This is your first time.

439
00:15:44,561 --> 00:15:45,620
- This is understandable. - Yes.

440
00:15:45,621 --> 00:15:46,630
(Anticipating)

441
00:15:46,631 --> 00:15:48,531
She's saying it half-heartedly now.

442
00:15:50,031 --> 00:15:51,231
Why is it so black?

443
00:15:52,361 --> 00:15:54,100
- The water could turn black... - What's this?

444
00:15:54,101 --> 00:15:55,701
- if you had never washed your car. - Yes.

445
00:15:56,571 --> 00:15:59,441
(He doesn't stop scrubbing his car.)

446
00:16:00,641 --> 00:16:02,770
(Dripping with dirty water)

447
00:16:02,771 --> 00:16:04,240
- Your truck is crying. - My gosh.

448
00:16:04,241 --> 00:16:05,610
- You must feel so bad... - Joy...

449
00:16:05,611 --> 00:16:07,311
- Right. I really felt bad. - for your truck.

450
00:16:07,981 --> 00:16:09,781
Gosh, I was shocked. Seriously.

451
00:16:10,651 --> 00:16:12,621
I really thought Damarghini...

452
00:16:12,951 --> 00:16:14,351
was possessed by an evil spirit.

453
00:16:14,921 --> 00:16:18,121
Seriously. How could water turn that black?

454
00:16:18,461 --> 00:16:19,861
Seriously. The black water...

455
00:16:20,731 --> 00:16:21,891
I was like, "What's this?"

456
00:16:22,531 --> 00:16:25,801
I thought water would turn that dark after smokey eye makeup.

457
00:16:28,331 --> 00:16:29,970
I'm inside!

458
00:16:29,971 --> 00:16:31,640
It looks like your truck is really crying.

459
00:16:31,641 --> 00:16:34,440
Right. The more I scrubbed it, the more dirty water came out.

460
00:16:34,441 --> 00:16:36,311
- You must perform an exorcism. - Right.

461
00:16:37,041 --> 00:16:38,580
The dirty water kept coming out.

462
00:16:38,581 --> 00:16:40,451
I had to scrub it.

463
00:16:40,581 --> 00:16:42,651
So I kept scrubbing. It didn't seem to end.

464
00:16:42,881 --> 00:16:45,780
This could be a chance to reflect on your behavior too.

465
00:16:45,781 --> 00:16:46,851
Of course.

466
00:16:47,021 --> 00:16:48,621
- Slowly, she's... - She's telling you to reflect.

467
00:16:48,991 --> 00:16:51,020
- That was the point. Right? - Yes.

468
00:16:51,021 --> 00:16:52,360
It might be better to say...

469
00:16:52,361 --> 00:16:53,661
- an evil spirit possessed his car. - Yes.

470
00:16:54,231 --> 00:16:57,131
(Let me see.)

471
00:16:59,201 --> 00:17:00,771
(Wiping)

472
00:17:01,631 --> 00:17:05,041
(He tries to gather the black tears with care.)

473
00:17:07,341 --> 00:17:08,910
- Why did you save that? - Why did you do that?

474
00:17:08,911 --> 00:17:09,940
- What are you doing? - Why?

475
00:17:09,941 --> 00:17:11,310
I needed more detergent...

476
00:17:11,311 --> 00:17:12,681
- for the top of my truck. - I see. For the top.

477
00:17:13,311 --> 00:17:15,411
I thought you would take that home and use it while you took a shower.

478
00:17:15,481 --> 00:17:16,880
- Me too. I really thought... - He's gathering that,

479
00:17:16,881 --> 00:17:19,250
- so he can wash dishes at home. - My gosh.

480
00:17:19,251 --> 00:17:20,320
You're a planner.

481
00:17:20,321 --> 00:17:22,221
- Yes. - He's got a plan and tricks.

482
00:17:23,591 --> 00:17:25,360
(He gathers every precious drop of it.)

483
00:17:25,361 --> 00:17:26,960
- Look. That's a lot. - Gosh.

484
00:17:26,961 --> 00:17:28,630
- It'd be a waste not to use it. - Gosh.

485
00:17:28,631 --> 00:17:32,331
(He sprinkles the black tears to the top of his truck.)

486
00:17:33,301 --> 00:17:35,631
I must do it right when I do it. This is exhausting.

487
00:17:38,241 --> 00:17:39,940
Let's clean it thoroughly.

488
00:17:39,941 --> 00:17:41,610
(With the collected black tears...)

489
00:17:41,611 --> 00:17:42,970
I'm done scrubbing off the dirt.

490
00:17:42,971 --> 00:17:44,141
(he finishes scrubbing the truck with detergent.)

491
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:50,451
Gosh, I must pay again.

492
00:17:52,751 --> 00:17:54,290
- Sir. - You ran out, right?

493
00:17:54,291 --> 00:17:55,951
Yes. Top up 20 more dollars, please.

494
00:17:56,721 --> 00:17:58,560
It must be because this is your first time.

495
00:17:58,561 --> 00:18:00,561
Usually, it doesn't cost this much.

496
00:18:00,661 --> 00:18:01,661
- Is that so? - Yes.

497
00:18:01,662 --> 00:18:02,690
How much does it usually cost?

498
00:18:02,691 --> 00:18:04,900
It usually costs 10 to 12 dollars.

499
00:18:04,901 --> 00:18:05,901
- Right. - Really?

500
00:18:05,902 --> 00:18:08,430
- Usually, yes. - Dads usually finish it...

501
00:18:08,431 --> 00:18:09,600
around ten dollars.

502
00:18:09,601 --> 00:18:11,670
I thought about it, but it's impossible to finish it...

503
00:18:11,671 --> 00:18:12,970
- only with ten dollars. - You need to know...

504
00:18:12,971 --> 00:18:14,411
exactly where to go and how to spray it.

505
00:18:15,841 --> 00:18:17,781
How can any finish this with ten dollars?

506
00:18:19,641 --> 00:18:20,651
Wash?

507
00:18:26,321 --> 00:18:27,690
What's that? Look at that.

508
00:18:27,691 --> 00:18:29,190
Look! He damaged the paint.

509
00:18:29,191 --> 00:18:30,791
See? It's got marks now.

510
00:18:31,961 --> 00:18:32,991
What? What happened here?

511
00:18:36,361 --> 00:18:37,861
You'll have to wash it again.

512
00:18:38,431 --> 00:18:39,761
But it looks dirtier.

513
00:18:40,131 --> 00:18:42,801
I think Damarghini is possessed by an evil spirit.

514
00:18:46,041 --> 00:18:48,941
(Teary-eyed)

515
00:18:50,011 --> 00:18:51,640
Why does it look dirtier?

516
00:18:51,641 --> 00:18:52,811
(What happened to my truck?)

517
00:18:53,811 --> 00:18:54,851
(Deducting 4 dollars)

518
00:18:55,081 --> 00:18:57,420
He's using detergent again. Oh, no!

519
00:18:57,421 --> 00:18:58,481
Again?

520
00:18:59,181 --> 00:19:01,151
At this rate, it'll cost as much as his truck.

521
00:19:03,151 --> 00:19:06,090
(He washes his truck...)

522
00:19:06,091 --> 00:19:08,391
(nonstop.)

523
00:19:09,091 --> 00:19:11,900
(But the black tear stains won't come off.)

524
00:19:11,901 --> 00:19:14,431
- It's coming from the rubber. - Yes.

525
00:19:15,971 --> 00:19:18,501
(Sighing)

526
00:19:20,141 --> 00:19:21,641
Why do I feel bad?

527
00:19:28,811 --> 00:19:30,580
(Insufficient fund)

528
00:19:30,581 --> 00:19:31,681
He ran out?

529
00:19:32,021 --> 00:19:33,251
How much money did I spend?

530
00:19:33,921 --> 00:19:35,291
I'm blowing up my money here.

531
00:19:36,291 --> 00:19:38,091
(Sweating profusely)

532
00:19:40,961 --> 00:19:43,930
Why does my truck keep dripping with black water?

533
00:19:43,931 --> 00:19:45,200
I noticed that it was coming...

534
00:19:45,201 --> 00:19:46,430
- from the rubber strips. - Yes.

535
00:19:46,431 --> 00:19:48,030
- The rubber strips are old. - I see.

536
00:19:48,031 --> 00:19:49,630
- When you scrub them, - It's from the rubber strips.

537
00:19:49,631 --> 00:19:51,271
- Yes. - Yes.

538
00:19:52,701 --> 00:19:53,810
Here you go.

539
00:19:53,811 --> 00:19:54,811
- Thank you. - Seventy dollars?

540
00:19:54,812 --> 00:19:56,541
- Okay. - It costs more than regular ones.

541
00:19:57,341 --> 00:19:58,410
(Stopping)

542
00:19:58,411 --> 00:20:00,081
Can I have some water?

543
00:20:00,251 --> 00:20:01,750
- Sure. - I was so thirsty.

544
00:20:01,751 --> 00:20:03,180
- Thank you. - Pay ten dollars.

545
00:20:03,181 --> 00:20:04,751
You should've tapped the card for drinking water.

546
00:20:04,821 --> 00:20:06,281
- Seriously. - "That's 20 dollars."

547
00:20:11,861 --> 00:20:13,861
I bet you dropped 3kg the next day.

548
00:20:15,661 --> 00:20:17,261
It was because of the rubber strips.

549
00:20:18,961 --> 00:20:20,071
My gosh.

550
00:20:21,431 --> 00:20:22,601
Oh, that.

551
00:20:24,371 --> 00:20:26,600
I can use the foam brush.

552
00:20:26,601 --> 00:20:29,070
I wonder why he didn't think to use that up until now.

553
00:20:29,071 --> 00:20:30,481
- Right. - The foam brush.

554
00:20:31,981 --> 00:20:33,111
The foam brush.

555
00:20:37,551 --> 00:20:39,180
- I like that. - That's nice.

556
00:20:39,181 --> 00:20:40,321
- That's a great tool. - My gosh.

557
00:20:41,851 --> 00:20:42,851
My gosh.

558
00:20:43,891 --> 00:20:45,021
Yes, this is it.

559
00:20:46,931 --> 00:20:48,990
- It's working now. - It got so easy with that.

560
00:20:48,991 --> 00:20:50,361
- Yes. - That looks convenient.

561
00:20:51,361 --> 00:20:53,970
With that, you didn't have to collect the foam for the top.

562
00:20:53,971 --> 00:20:54,971
- Yes. - Right.

563
00:20:57,241 --> 00:20:58,701
(Deducting 4 dollars)

564
00:20:59,441 --> 00:21:02,511
(He's using the water hose at the same time.)

565
00:21:03,371 --> 00:21:04,381
I can do this.

566
00:21:05,141 --> 00:21:06,750
- I started to get the hang of it. - If you left it for a long time,

567
00:21:06,751 --> 00:21:08,050
it might leave a stain?

568
00:21:08,051 --> 00:21:09,281
- I got it. - Yes, that's why.

569
00:21:09,381 --> 00:21:10,650
The dirt didn't come out if I didn't scrub it.

570
00:21:10,651 --> 00:21:11,881
It came out only when I scrubbed it.

571
00:21:15,021 --> 00:21:17,191
(Giggling)

572
00:21:17,961 --> 00:21:19,060
It's working.

573
00:21:19,061 --> 00:21:21,491
(Damarghini is gradually turning white.)

574
00:21:23,461 --> 00:21:25,230
It felt great to watch my truck...

575
00:21:25,231 --> 00:21:26,431
getting cleaned.

576
00:21:27,601 --> 00:21:28,631
Gosh, this is exhausting.

577
00:21:29,371 --> 00:21:30,441
Did it improve?

578
00:21:31,041 --> 00:21:32,541
It's gotten cleaner.

579
00:21:33,911 --> 00:21:35,610
By the way, it looks really clean.

580
00:21:35,611 --> 00:21:36,881
(Damarghini is crying less now.)

581
00:21:38,081 --> 00:21:40,410
- It looks clean now. - He's finally pulling out his car.

582
00:21:40,411 --> 00:21:42,451
(He has to wipe the moisture outside the booth.)

583
00:21:44,481 --> 00:21:46,421
Gosh, washing a car isn't an easy task.

584
00:21:53,161 --> 00:21:54,261
I must take everything.

585
00:21:57,501 --> 00:21:59,000
I had to clean up after myself.

586
00:21:59,001 --> 00:22:00,671
(He picks up all of his trash and takes it with him.)

587
00:22:05,241 --> 00:22:06,700
- I see. The foam? - What?

588
00:22:06,701 --> 00:22:07,941
(He's spraying water on the ground?)

589
00:22:08,041 --> 00:22:09,740
Did you spend money to clean up?

590
00:22:09,741 --> 00:22:11,840
Do you have to wash the ground afterward?

591
00:22:11,841 --> 00:22:13,311
- You don't have to do that. - People don't do that.

592
00:22:13,881 --> 00:22:15,111
The thing is,

593
00:22:15,281 --> 00:22:16,580
a truly beautiful person makes...

594
00:22:16,581 --> 00:22:17,981
- wherever they stay look beautiful. - Right.

595
00:22:18,651 --> 00:22:21,520
The dirty water from Damarghini...

596
00:22:21,521 --> 00:22:23,721
was darker than I thought.

597
00:22:24,191 --> 00:22:26,221
I rinsed the booth as a matter of etiquette.

598
00:22:26,861 --> 00:22:28,030
- So... - Dae Ho, clean your house...

599
00:22:28,031 --> 00:22:29,160
with that attitude.

600
00:22:29,161 --> 00:22:30,961
(Dae Ho, clean your house with that attitude.)

601
00:22:35,271 --> 00:22:36,671
But we ought to learn that from you.

602
00:22:36,871 --> 00:22:38,200
You should wash the owner's back too.

603
00:22:38,201 --> 00:22:39,241
That's right.

604
00:22:39,701 --> 00:22:41,541
That's right. You should do that.

605
00:22:41,871 --> 00:22:44,141
(He washes the top of the car thoroughly.)

606
00:22:44,741 --> 00:22:46,781
(He wipes off the remaining water.)

607
00:22:48,081 --> 00:22:50,010
(Groaning)

608
00:22:50,011 --> 00:22:51,081
This is nice.

609
00:22:53,621 --> 00:22:55,921
(Is this the end?)

610
00:22:59,721 --> 00:23:00,831
Gosh.

611
00:23:02,191 --> 00:23:03,231
Gosh.

612
00:23:03,801 --> 00:23:04,831
I'm done.

613
00:23:05,701 --> 00:23:07,931
Why don't you clean the interior of the van?

614
00:23:08,401 --> 00:23:09,530
Cleaning the interior...

615
00:23:09,531 --> 00:23:11,141
It'll take him 1 night and 2 days to clean the interior of the van.

616
00:23:12,841 --> 00:23:13,871
All done.

617
00:23:15,671 --> 00:23:19,841
(Let's leave behind the past of getting covered in plants.)

618
00:23:21,011 --> 00:23:22,510
I washed the van for hours.

619
00:23:22,511 --> 00:23:23,881
(Damarghini got a wash for the 1st time in 5 years.)

620
00:23:25,851 --> 00:23:27,421
It's clean.

621
00:23:29,091 --> 00:23:30,091
What?

622
00:23:30,291 --> 00:23:31,690
That always happens.

623
00:23:31,691 --> 00:23:32,791
What's that?

624
00:23:34,591 --> 00:23:36,260
Why didn't you remove that?

625
00:23:36,261 --> 00:23:37,360
What's up with the leaf?

626
00:23:37,361 --> 00:23:39,560
He left it like a bookmark.

627
00:23:39,561 --> 00:23:41,330
- It's like a hair streak. - "I read it up to here."

628
00:23:41,331 --> 00:23:42,701
It's romance.

629
00:23:43,641 --> 00:23:44,940
I feel refreshed.

630
00:23:44,941 --> 00:23:46,271
(It's refreshing and nice.)

631
00:23:46,911 --> 00:23:47,911
(Total time: 1 hour and 35 minutes, Total cost: 68 dollars)

632
00:23:47,912 --> 00:23:49,110
It looks clean.

633
00:23:49,111 --> 00:23:50,381
My goodness.

634
00:23:50,611 --> 00:23:52,010
You wasted your time.

635
00:23:52,011 --> 00:23:53,881
- This is driving me crazy. - You wasted your time.

636
00:23:54,511 --> 00:23:56,381
It gives you a strange sense of accomplishment.

637
00:23:56,581 --> 00:23:58,521
Just think that you paid for a sense of accomplishment.

638
00:23:58,681 --> 00:24:01,790
I got to relieve my feeling of guilt regarding Damarghini.

639
00:24:01,791 --> 00:24:03,351
That's right. You paid for a sense of accomplishment.

640
00:24:04,061 --> 00:24:06,620
I feel refreshed.

641
00:24:06,621 --> 00:24:08,231
(Feeling refreshed, he hits the road.)

642
00:24:10,031 --> 00:24:11,100
I'm home.

643
00:24:11,101 --> 00:24:12,101
(Sweet home)

644
00:24:12,861 --> 00:24:13,970
It's clean.

645
00:24:13,971 --> 00:24:15,631
(The car wash outing was pretty refreshing.)

646
00:24:15,931 --> 00:24:17,571
All right.

647
00:24:19,171 --> 00:24:23,010
(He goes to House 2 as he hums a tune.)

648
00:24:23,011 --> 00:24:24,641
(Turning on the light)

649
00:24:25,311 --> 00:24:26,711
The bathtub is nice.

650
00:24:26,911 --> 00:24:28,851
- I love that room. - That room is so nice.

651
00:24:29,281 --> 00:24:31,421
- His house is so clean. - It's nice.

652
00:24:32,921 --> 00:24:34,650
(The comic book room that's full of dreams...)

653
00:24:34,651 --> 00:24:35,791
I feel a sense of accomplishment.

654
00:24:36,991 --> 00:24:38,090
(got more comic books.)

655
00:24:38,091 --> 00:24:40,161
- You're maintaining it well. - I'm using it well.

656
00:24:40,991 --> 00:24:42,961
(The innovative liquor room)

657
00:24:44,431 --> 00:24:46,161
I see many more liquors.

658
00:24:47,501 --> 00:24:48,701
What happened to the movie room?

659
00:24:49,101 --> 00:24:51,641
- That isn't half bad. - Sometimes, I sleep there.

660
00:24:55,271 --> 00:24:58,180
(Wearing slippers, he enters...)

661
00:24:58,181 --> 00:24:59,181
(the vivarium room.)

662
00:24:59,182 --> 00:25:00,481
You haven't killed them off.

663
00:25:01,111 --> 00:25:02,310
I see more vivariums.

664
00:25:02,311 --> 00:25:03,821
I'm doing my absolute best to fill the tanks.

665
00:25:04,981 --> 00:25:07,050
(His vivariums were either dead...)

666
00:25:07,051 --> 00:25:09,021
(or empty.)

667
00:25:10,361 --> 00:25:11,691
They're growing nicely.

668
00:25:12,221 --> 00:25:13,591
He's a true expert.

669
00:25:14,331 --> 00:25:15,490
He has set them up so nicely.

670
00:25:15,491 --> 00:25:16,631
- Oh, my. - My goodness.

671
00:25:17,401 --> 00:25:18,500
It's a salamander.

672
00:25:18,501 --> 00:25:20,030
(Cute friends have been added.)

673
00:25:20,031 --> 00:25:21,071
There are a lot.

674
00:25:25,441 --> 00:25:27,770
(He puts down the pieces of wood he found in the vivarium room.)

675
00:25:27,771 --> 00:25:29,011
- There are many such items. - What are those?

676
00:25:29,171 --> 00:25:30,510
Will you turn your house into a vivarium?

677
00:25:30,511 --> 00:25:31,511
No.

678
00:25:31,512 --> 00:25:32,541
(No way)

679
00:25:33,581 --> 00:25:35,181
I need to create borders.

680
00:25:37,451 --> 00:25:39,821
(He pulls out a chunk of clay.)

681
00:25:40,921 --> 00:25:42,151
What's that?

682
00:25:42,451 --> 00:25:44,761
- His house will become a vivarium! - I guess so.

683
00:25:44,921 --> 00:25:47,260
- He wants to be a salamander. - Will you become a salamander?

684
00:25:47,261 --> 00:25:48,491
He wants to be a salamander.

685
00:25:49,061 --> 00:25:50,631
Maybe he'll stick to the wall.

686
00:25:51,661 --> 00:25:52,701
All done.

687
00:25:53,101 --> 00:25:55,401
(As the panelists speculate, he finishes the wooden border.)

688
00:25:56,301 --> 00:25:58,271
(Opening)

689
00:26:00,911 --> 00:26:02,210
- What's that? - What's that?

690
00:26:02,211 --> 00:26:03,211
Is it moss?

691
00:26:03,741 --> 00:26:05,481
It's impossible to predict what's inside.

692
00:26:06,711 --> 00:26:07,711
(Gosh!)

693
00:26:08,111 --> 00:26:11,451
(He works his muscles to bring over a mysterious box.)

694
00:26:12,651 --> 00:26:15,421
(The boxes pile up.)

695
00:26:19,821 --> 00:26:20,860
Oh, my!

696
00:26:20,861 --> 00:26:21,890
(The light suddenly goes out.)

697
00:26:21,891 --> 00:26:22,891
Oh, my!

698
00:26:22,892 --> 00:26:24,031
What's going on?

699
00:26:24,101 --> 00:26:25,230
(What?)

700
00:26:25,231 --> 00:26:26,431
It's a short circuit.

701
00:26:29,301 --> 00:26:31,241
I set up electricity again,

702
00:26:31,441 --> 00:26:34,641
but there was a leak when it rained a lot.

703
00:26:35,171 --> 00:26:36,441
Whenever I turned on the air conditioner,

704
00:26:36,871 --> 00:26:39,811
the circuit breaker tripped after 10 to 15 minutes.

705
00:26:40,511 --> 00:26:41,650
Now that I've lived here for a while,

706
00:26:41,651 --> 00:26:43,411
I think living in a house is harder in summer than in winter.

707
00:26:44,051 --> 00:26:45,281
You have two options.

708
00:26:45,621 --> 00:26:47,691
You can either maintain the house meticulously and diligently...

709
00:26:47,951 --> 00:26:49,821
like Na Rae or KEY...

710
00:26:51,021 --> 00:26:52,521
or leave the house alone like me.

711
00:26:53,931 --> 00:26:56,031
You need to fall into 1 of those 2 categories.

712
00:26:56,391 --> 00:26:57,830
If you're an in-betweener, living in a house will be hard.

713
00:26:57,831 --> 00:26:59,131
It's definitely like that.

714
00:27:00,401 --> 00:27:02,070
Given President Jun's tendencies,

715
00:27:02,071 --> 00:27:05,140
he'll struggle if he lives in a house.

716
00:27:05,141 --> 00:27:06,870
I know what he can do.

717
00:27:06,871 --> 00:27:10,311
Why doesn't he have a trial period by living in a small house?

718
00:27:11,511 --> 00:27:12,781
No place beats my house.

719
00:27:13,281 --> 00:27:14,711
If President Jun is...

720
00:27:15,881 --> 00:27:17,451
open to a short-term rental,

721
00:27:17,821 --> 00:27:20,221
I want to try living in an apartment.

722
00:27:21,251 --> 00:27:24,961
President Jun and I could switch places for a day.

723
00:27:25,891 --> 00:27:28,530
I can't imagine Dae Ho in that apartment.

724
00:27:28,531 --> 00:27:30,031
- I know. - I want to see him in that setting.

725
00:27:30,801 --> 00:27:32,231
What have I done to deserve that?

726
00:27:32,731 --> 00:27:34,571
- Nothing. - You wanted to live in a house!

727
00:27:34,701 --> 00:27:36,070
Why do I need to live in an abandoned house?

728
00:27:36,071 --> 00:27:37,640
- I mean... - Why do I need to do that?

729
00:27:37,641 --> 00:27:38,840
Dae Ho lives there!

730
00:27:38,841 --> 00:27:39,870
Why do I need to live in an abandoned house?

731
00:27:39,871 --> 00:27:40,970
- Dae Ho lives there! - Don't call it an abandoned house.

732
00:27:40,971 --> 00:27:42,941
He lives there.

733
00:27:43,071 --> 00:27:44,380
- An abandoned house! - It looks more abandoned...

734
00:27:44,381 --> 00:27:45,480
- than an abandoned house. - Don't call it that.

735
00:27:45,481 --> 00:27:46,910
Dae Ho lives there.

736
00:27:46,911 --> 00:27:48,211
It's an occupied house.

737
00:27:49,181 --> 00:27:52,251
On the deck outside,

738
00:27:52,481 --> 00:27:55,391
I'll leave out some tasks for him.

739
00:27:55,921 --> 00:27:57,221
It'll be nice if he does them.

740
00:27:57,561 --> 00:27:59,020
It's a good idea.

741
00:27:59,021 --> 00:28:00,021
It's an exclusive offer for President Jun.

742
00:28:00,022 --> 00:28:01,091
Right.

743
00:28:01,331 --> 00:28:02,631
For goodness' sake.

744
00:28:03,661 --> 00:28:05,201
The hotter, the better.

745
00:28:05,731 --> 00:28:08,031
How could you tell me to live there when the electricity is out?

746
00:28:10,371 --> 00:28:12,241
(I'll fight heat with heat!)

747
00:28:13,341 --> 00:28:14,341
(He moves the heavy boxes without resting.)

748
00:28:14,341 --> 00:28:15,341
The last one.

749
00:28:15,771 --> 00:28:17,441
He's doing that without air conditioning.

750
00:28:18,581 --> 00:28:20,751
(The place is full of boxes.)

751
00:28:21,981 --> 00:28:24,451
(He finally reveals what's inside the box.)

752
00:28:25,521 --> 00:28:27,591
(Heave-ho)

753
00:28:29,391 --> 00:28:30,721
- It's rice. - Clay?

754
00:28:30,891 --> 00:28:32,660
- Rice! - What?

755
00:28:32,661 --> 00:28:34,360
- It looks like clay. - What is he doing?

756
00:28:34,361 --> 00:28:35,631
What on earth is he doing?

757
00:28:36,731 --> 00:28:38,901
(Mysterious substance in white is piled up.)

758
00:28:42,201 --> 00:28:43,831
(Shall I open it now?)

759
00:28:46,001 --> 00:28:47,001
(Sand pours out.)

760
00:28:47,002 --> 00:28:48,111
What?

761
00:28:48,741 --> 00:28:49,811
What a lunatic!

762
00:28:51,441 --> 00:28:52,511
What a lunatic!

763
00:28:54,851 --> 00:28:55,950
(Dae Ho, come on.)

764
00:28:55,951 --> 00:28:57,281
This is actually insane.

765
00:28:58,412 --> 00:29:00,181
(Sand pours out to the floor.)

766
00:29:00,182 --> 00:29:01,182
No way.

767
00:29:01,582 --> 00:29:03,682
(Grinning)

768
00:29:04,312 --> 00:29:05,351
(Giggling)

769
00:29:05,352 --> 00:29:06,652
He's crazy about entertainment.

770
00:29:07,122 --> 00:29:09,482
(Giggling)

771
00:29:10,492 --> 00:29:13,822
(It looked like he had chased away the evil spirit of Damarghini.)

772
00:29:14,892 --> 00:29:17,062
(Cutting)

773
00:29:17,762 --> 00:29:18,762
(Laughing like a maniac)

774
00:29:18,763 --> 00:29:20,732
- What on earth are you doing? - Seriously.

775
00:29:23,232 --> 00:29:24,771
(Did the evil spirit possess Dae Ho this time?)

776
00:29:24,772 --> 00:29:25,872
I can't believe it.

777
00:29:26,842 --> 00:29:28,001
It really must be bad spirit.

778
00:29:28,002 --> 00:29:29,041
(How scary)

779
00:29:29,042 --> 00:29:31,212
In my house, I'll make the feature that has been a long-cherished wish.

780
00:29:31,572 --> 00:29:33,111
I'll make a beach.

781
00:29:33,112 --> 00:29:34,541
- I see. - I see.

782
00:29:34,542 --> 00:29:36,612
(A beach?)

783
00:29:36,782 --> 00:29:39,552
- You know, you should do it once. - That's right.

