1546
00:59:00,142 --> 00:59:01,212
(License qualification)

1547
00:59:01,642 --> 00:59:02,912
I'm taking a driving test.

1548
00:59:03,182 --> 00:59:05,181
- On that day? - Yes. On that day.

1549
00:59:05,182 --> 00:59:07,151
- The driving test? - For the written test,

1550
00:59:07,152 --> 00:59:08,152
(Showing)

1551
00:59:08,153 --> 00:59:09,351
I've already passed.

1552
00:59:09,352 --> 00:59:11,222
I heard that the written test was hard these days.

1553
00:59:11,622 --> 00:59:12,891
I worked hard to study...

1554
00:59:12,892 --> 00:59:15,422
and passed with quite a high score.

1555
00:59:15,862 --> 00:59:16,922
Nice one.

1556
00:59:17,662 --> 00:59:20,892
I wanted to get the Class One license.

1557
00:59:21,292 --> 00:59:22,501
I heard it was hard to get the Class One license.

1558
00:59:22,502 --> 00:59:23,802
Class One Manual?

1559
00:59:24,262 --> 00:59:25,572
- Automatic. - I see.

1560
00:59:27,032 --> 00:59:29,142
(Class 2, Class 1)

1561
00:59:29,542 --> 00:59:31,542
(Unlike Class 2, where the yellow cars are driven,)

1562
00:59:31,972 --> 00:59:33,211
(a 1-ton truck is driven for Class 1.)

1563
00:59:33,212 --> 00:59:35,212
Is Class 1 a lot more difficult than Class 2?

1564
00:59:35,612 --> 00:59:37,342
- I heard it was really difficult. - Don't even talk about it.

1565
00:59:38,182 --> 00:59:40,351
- I drove the big car in Turkiye. - Right.

1566
00:59:40,352 --> 00:59:42,081
- There are times when it is needed. - Right.

1567
00:59:42,082 --> 00:59:44,421
Do all of you have a driver's license?

1568
00:59:44,422 --> 00:59:45,551
I have a Class Two license.

1569
00:59:45,552 --> 00:59:46,691
- Same here. - Same here.

1570
00:59:46,692 --> 00:59:49,462
Isn't Hyun Moo the only one here with a Class One license?

1571
00:59:49,592 --> 00:59:51,361
- Class One Ordinary. - Right.

1572
00:59:51,362 --> 00:59:52,731
Many around our age got the Class One Ordinary license.

1573
00:59:52,732 --> 00:59:53,991
- Really? - Back then, anything else...

1574
00:59:53,992 --> 00:59:55,402
- wasn't considered a real license. - Right.

1575
00:59:55,762 --> 00:59:57,261
It's all about changing gears.

1576
00:59:57,262 --> 00:59:58,901
- Right. - Class Two was looked down on.

1577
00:59:58,902 --> 01:00:00,331
- I see. - "Isn't that for toy cars?"

1578
01:00:00,332 --> 01:00:01,371
- This was what was said. - Right.

1579
01:00:01,372 --> 01:00:03,602
- A license for bumper cars. - Bumper cars?

1580
01:00:04,242 --> 01:00:06,642
It reeks of boomers here.

1581
01:00:07,342 --> 01:00:10,041
- It reeks of boomers? - Yes.

1582
01:00:10,042 --> 01:00:12,511
Driving must be done like a boomer though.

1583
01:00:12,512 --> 01:00:13,552
Of course.

1584
01:00:14,112 --> 01:00:16,022
The biggest reason for wanting to get a license...

1585
01:00:16,182 --> 01:00:18,122
was because I was Dudu's owner.

1586
01:00:18,422 --> 01:00:20,691
- "What if Dudu gets sick?" - That's a big reason.

1587
01:00:20,692 --> 01:00:24,821
If I have to take my dog to the hospital urgently,

1588
01:00:24,822 --> 01:00:27,631
I can't take a taxi with him in my arms.

1589
01:00:27,632 --> 01:00:29,101
I can only take the pet taxi.

1590
01:00:29,102 --> 01:00:32,372
That was why I thought I had to have a driver's license.

1591
01:00:34,032 --> 01:00:35,372
Listen up, Dudu.

1592
01:00:37,402 --> 01:00:39,112
I'll go and take my driving test.

1593
01:00:42,542 --> 01:00:43,941
(One last hug before leaving)

1594
01:00:43,942 --> 01:00:45,182
I'll give you a hug.

1595
01:00:45,482 --> 01:00:47,152
- Look at him leaning on her. - I'll go and do my best.

1596
01:00:48,012 --> 01:00:49,381
I'll make sure to do well.

1597
01:00:49,382 --> 01:00:51,281
You're trying to keep yourself calm, right?

1598
01:00:51,282 --> 01:00:52,852
Yes. I felt so nervous.

1599
01:00:54,122 --> 01:00:55,561
So people get nervous for automatic licenses too.

1600
01:00:55,562 --> 01:00:57,022
(Laughing)

1601
01:00:57,662 --> 01:00:59,332
Bye, Dudu!

1602
01:00:59,792 --> 01:01:01,462
I'll go and drive a truck.

1603
01:01:03,332 --> 01:01:04,561
She must feel so nervous!

1604
01:01:04,562 --> 01:01:07,002
(I'll come back after passing my test.)

1605
01:01:07,872 --> 01:01:11,912
(The taxi she called for arrives.)

1606
01:01:13,142 --> 01:01:14,772
- Hello. - Welcome.

1607
01:01:15,682 --> 01:01:16,941
Thank you, sir.

1608
01:01:16,942 --> 01:01:18,951
So there are tests during the day as well.

1609
01:01:18,952 --> 01:01:20,781
Right. Tests can be taken at different times these days.

1610
01:01:20,782 --> 01:01:22,252
I went early in the morning.

1611
01:01:24,652 --> 01:01:26,491
(Her heart is beating quickly.)

1612
01:01:26,492 --> 01:01:27,651
I'm feeling so nervous.

1613
01:01:27,652 --> 01:01:29,362
I took an ox bezoar pill.

1614
01:01:29,992 --> 01:01:31,792
I'm feeling nervous too.

1615
01:01:33,962 --> 01:01:36,632
I was getting crazy nervous from there.

1616
01:01:36,832 --> 01:01:39,132
I think it's better to get a license in summer.

1617
01:01:39,532 --> 01:01:40,631
Why?

1618
01:01:40,632 --> 01:01:42,142
Strangely, you get more nervous in winter.

1619
01:01:42,402 --> 01:01:44,072
- Because it's too cold. - Your hands freeze.

1620
01:01:44,472 --> 01:01:46,011
- That's because it's cold. - That's only natural!

1621
01:01:46,012 --> 01:01:47,671
- You're saying the obvious. - No, it's...

1622
01:01:47,672 --> 01:01:49,381
- I get what you mean. - You get it, right?

1623
01:01:49,382 --> 01:01:50,681
- I get what he means. - I mean...

1624
01:01:50,682 --> 01:01:51,951
You don't start right away for the practical test.

1625
01:01:51,952 --> 01:01:53,682
- You have to wait for your turn. - It gets cold.

1626
01:01:53,782 --> 01:01:55,111
Because it was cold and I was nervous,

1627
01:01:55,112 --> 01:01:57,222
I kept shaking, when I'm not the type to.

1628
01:01:57,382 --> 01:01:59,622
- That's right! It... - I remember shaking like this.

1629
01:01:59,722 --> 01:02:01,022
- It affects you. - That's right.

1630
01:02:01,252 --> 01:02:02,461
- I know. - Did you all pass...

1631
01:02:02,462 --> 01:02:03,662
the practical test at once?

1632
01:02:03,792 --> 01:02:04,821
- I... - I passed at once.

1633
01:02:04,822 --> 01:02:05,931
I passed at once too.

1634
01:02:05,932 --> 01:02:07,032
I failed, though.

1635
01:02:07,292 --> 01:02:08,761
I failed too.

1636
01:02:08,762 --> 01:02:11,931
When you fail the practical test, they announce it so loudly...

1637
01:02:11,932 --> 01:02:13,932
- that it's humiliating. - I know.

1638
01:02:14,032 --> 01:02:15,972
They couldn't have gone, "Joy of Red Velvet, you failed."

1639
01:02:16,342 --> 01:02:18,142
- "Joy of Red Velvet?" - But...

1640
01:02:18,302 --> 01:02:19,371
Red flavor

1641
01:02:19,372 --> 01:02:20,472
- Joy. - Red flavor

1642
01:02:20,742 --> 01:02:22,141
You failed

1643
01:02:22,142 --> 01:02:24,882
- Everyone there... - Red flavor, you failed

1644
01:02:25,212 --> 01:02:26,312
But...

1645
01:02:28,582 --> 01:02:31,382
(Exploding with red flavor that makes your face go red)

1646
01:02:32,022 --> 01:02:36,262
(After driving for a while, she almost reached her destination.)

1647
01:02:36,392 --> 01:02:37,722
When you turn left or right...

1648
01:02:37,922 --> 01:02:42,262
(Suddenly getting nervous)

1649
01:02:43,362 --> 01:02:45,831
(Worried)

1650
01:02:45,832 --> 01:02:48,002
- It makes you really nervous. - I was really nervous.

1651
01:02:48,772 --> 01:02:50,442
I feel like throwing up, watching this.

1652
01:02:51,072 --> 01:02:52,472
You're here.

1653
01:02:53,142 --> 01:02:54,812
- Thank you. - Sure.

1654
01:02:55,042 --> 01:02:56,411
Have a good day.

1655
01:02:56,412 --> 01:02:58,012
(Today's destination she finally reached)

1656
01:02:59,652 --> 01:03:02,022
(She gets out filled with worries.)

1657
01:03:03,052 --> 01:03:05,322
(Plodding)

1658
01:03:06,352 --> 01:03:07,591
(She walks somewhere.)

1659
01:03:07,592 --> 01:03:08,722
What is this?

1660
01:03:09,492 --> 01:03:11,492
- Hello. - Hello.

1661
01:03:12,092 --> 01:03:13,162
What is that?

1662
01:03:14,992 --> 01:03:16,802
- Oh, my. - What is this?

1663
01:03:16,932 --> 01:03:21,402
It's a driving simulator training center that uses a screen.

1664
01:03:22,642 --> 01:03:26,111
(A center where you can practice using a simulator indoors)

1665
01:03:26,112 --> 01:03:27,611
- What a world we live in. - Oh, my.

1666
01:03:27,612 --> 01:03:28,711
That's fascinating.

1667
01:03:28,712 --> 01:03:32,752
The frame, gear shift, wheel, and everything else...

1668
01:03:32,912 --> 01:03:34,152
are exactly the same.

1669
01:03:34,482 --> 01:03:36,222
(People who dream of becoming the best drivers)

1670
01:03:36,952 --> 01:03:38,152
I thought I'd get less nervous...

1671
01:03:39,092 --> 01:03:42,291
when I drive a real car if I practiced with the simulator.

1672
01:03:42,292 --> 01:03:43,791
There was only so much you could learn from YouTube.

1673
01:03:43,792 --> 01:03:45,262
There was only so much I could ask too.

1674
01:03:45,592 --> 01:03:48,332
I went there yesterday too, and I practiced for four hours.

1675
01:03:49,062 --> 01:03:50,531
- Four hours? - Yes.

1676
01:03:50,532 --> 01:03:52,672
I drove to Busan using the simulator.

1677
01:03:52,832 --> 01:03:54,671
But you can get the license right away these days...

1678
01:03:54,672 --> 01:03:56,341
because there are so many well-made videos online.

1679
01:03:56,342 --> 01:03:57,572
- That's true. - Really?

1680
01:03:57,942 --> 01:04:00,242
I heard there were many people who studied on their own.

1681
01:04:01,712 --> 01:04:03,312
Gosh, I'm so nervous.

1682
01:04:04,642 --> 01:04:07,552
(She practices before taking the test.)

1683
01:04:08,652 --> 01:04:11,352
(Taking a seat)

1684
01:04:13,522 --> 01:04:14,821
After adjusting the seat...

1685
01:04:14,822 --> 01:04:16,692
(She adjusts the seat first.)

1686
01:04:17,522 --> 01:04:19,062
It's exactly the same as the test.

1687
01:04:19,392 --> 01:04:22,302
- Gosh, that's realistic. - How nerve-racking!

1688
01:04:22,632 --> 01:04:24,761
The time limit is 9 minutes and 50 seconds.

1689
01:04:24,762 --> 01:04:26,201
- That's right. - Oh, right.

1690
01:04:26,202 --> 01:04:27,601
- There's a time limit. - There's a time limit.

1691
01:04:27,602 --> 01:04:28,772
- I know. - Step on the brake.

1692
01:04:29,172 --> 01:04:31,802
When the needle goes up, it means the car's started.

1693
01:04:32,942 --> 01:04:34,472
We will begin now.

1694
01:04:34,772 --> 01:04:36,482
The voice sounds exactly the same.

1695
01:04:36,782 --> 01:04:38,082
Release the handbrake.

1696
01:04:38,582 --> 01:04:41,651
So it's really lifelike.

1697
01:04:41,652 --> 01:04:43,652
(Nervous)

1698
01:04:44,222 --> 01:04:46,021
Be careful not to go over 20km.

1699
01:04:46,022 --> 01:04:47,892
Then a green light will come on.

1700
01:04:48,722 --> 01:04:50,522
That's when you need to turn off the turn signal.

1701
01:04:50,792 --> 01:04:52,591
(Turning it off with one hand)

1702
01:04:52,592 --> 01:04:55,562
(Focused)

1703
01:04:55,862 --> 01:04:59,471
- Lower the speed by ten percent. - Yes, you need to go slowly.

1704
01:04:59,472 --> 01:05:01,372
- You should barely step on the gas. - From here...

1705
01:05:01,702 --> 01:05:03,002
Stop here for three seconds.

1706
01:05:03,672 --> 01:05:04,942
Check if it's been three seconds.

1707
01:05:05,302 --> 01:05:06,441
- Then you can go. - It's really nerve-racking...

1708
01:05:06,442 --> 01:05:07,542
not to step on the line.

1709
01:05:08,212 --> 01:05:11,542
(A left turn right in front)

1710
01:05:12,512 --> 01:05:13,651
You can even stop when you turn.

1711
01:05:13,652 --> 01:05:15,252
- She's pretty good. - Stop if it feels risky.

1712
01:05:16,052 --> 01:05:17,821
- Stop if it feels risky. - Oh, no!

1713
01:05:17,822 --> 01:05:19,091
(Disqualified)

1714
01:05:19,092 --> 01:05:20,192
What?

1715
01:05:20,522 --> 01:05:22,121
- You bumped into the wall? - Yes.

1716
01:05:22,122 --> 01:05:24,061
- How did you bump into it? - I mean...

1717
01:05:24,062 --> 01:05:26,392
I find turning left and right really hard.

1718
01:05:26,992 --> 01:05:29,201
I can't figure it out. How much I need to turn...

1719
01:05:29,202 --> 01:05:30,961
- How much you need to turn? - That's right.

1720
01:05:30,962 --> 01:05:32,331
How much I need to turn...

1721
01:05:32,332 --> 01:05:35,072
- at which point. - You can't call that turning left.

1722
01:05:35,272 --> 01:05:36,601
I really can't tell.

1723
01:05:36,602 --> 01:05:37,901
That's really important, though.

1724
01:05:37,902 --> 01:05:39,641
You're developing a sense for it.

1725
01:05:39,642 --> 01:05:40,942
That's the most difficult part.

1726
01:05:41,142 --> 01:05:42,181
(Disqualified)

1727
01:05:42,182 --> 01:05:43,681
You get disqualified right away if you bump into it?

1728
01:05:43,682 --> 01:05:45,182
Yes, you get disqualified right away.

1729
01:05:45,782 --> 01:05:46,912
It's so scary.

1730
01:05:47,812 --> 01:05:49,352
Fortunately, it'll get easier when you are there.

1731
01:05:50,682 --> 01:05:52,921
- This could be even more difficult. - That could be the case.

1732
01:05:52,922 --> 01:05:54,992
- That's why it's hard. - It's different from a real car.

1733
01:05:55,522 --> 01:05:57,422
(Turning)

1734
01:05:58,262 --> 01:05:59,532
You need to turn more.

1735
01:06:00,532 --> 01:06:02,201
- Disqualified. - Oh, you can tell right away...

1736
01:06:02,202 --> 01:06:03,762
- that I need to turn more. - Yes, you need to turn more.

1737
01:06:04,602 --> 01:06:05,802
You need to be careful of that.

1738
01:06:06,302 --> 01:06:09,042
(It's finally time for the T-shaped parking section.)

1739
01:06:09,442 --> 01:06:11,802
(Nervous)

1740
01:06:12,372 --> 01:06:14,411
(Turning right as she enters the parking space)

1741
01:06:14,412 --> 01:06:16,312
(Almost stepping on the line)

1742
01:06:16,612 --> 01:06:19,382
(Checking the side-view mirrors with sharp eyes)

1743
01:06:19,782 --> 01:06:21,152
(Shifting the gear to reverse)

1744
01:06:21,552 --> 01:06:24,722
(Carefully reversing while watching the line)

1745
01:06:26,952 --> 01:06:28,692
You can't step on the line.

1746
01:06:29,592 --> 01:06:33,262
(Lining up the tires with the parking line)

1747
01:06:33,332 --> 01:06:35,432
(Then she reverses straight.)

1748
01:06:36,702 --> 01:06:38,301
You're good. It's hard to park.

1749
01:06:38,302 --> 01:06:41,532
There were preset parking techniques I didn't know of.

1750
01:06:41,772 --> 01:06:43,072
Parallel parking is the difficult one.

1751
01:06:43,842 --> 01:06:46,041
- But it's not included, right? - It's not.

1752
01:06:46,042 --> 01:06:48,471
- There's no parallel parking? - There's no parallel parking?

1753
01:06:48,472 --> 01:06:51,042
Oh, my. You scared me.

1754
01:06:51,742 --> 01:06:53,482
- Seriously... - No parallel parking means...

1755
01:06:53,712 --> 01:06:54,981
- I can't approve of it. - I mean...

1756
01:06:54,982 --> 01:06:56,421
Do you think you'll do parallel parking more...

1757
01:06:56,422 --> 01:06:58,121
or T-shaped parking more when you're on the road?

1758
01:06:58,122 --> 01:06:59,491
- But these days, - You'll do parallel parking more.

1759
01:06:59,492 --> 01:07:00,822
parallel parking isn't included.

1760
01:07:00,992 --> 01:07:03,092
- There's only T-shaped parking. - Everyone, return your licenses.

1761
01:07:03,792 --> 01:07:05,421
- I had to do parallel parking. - I did too.

1762
01:07:05,422 --> 01:07:06,632
- I did too. - Then I approve of it.

1763
01:07:07,832 --> 01:07:09,501
Why must we get your approval?

1764
01:07:09,502 --> 01:07:10,561
- You're right. - Exactly.

1765
01:07:10,562 --> 01:07:11,661
- What is this? - I almost failed...

1766
01:07:11,662 --> 01:07:12,772
because of parallel parking.

1767
01:07:13,202 --> 01:07:14,402
It was really hard.

1768
01:07:15,202 --> 01:07:17,402
(Riding the momentum)

1769
01:07:17,872 --> 01:07:19,442
(Fumbling)

1770
01:07:19,942 --> 01:07:22,241
(Putting on glasses)

1771
01:07:22,242 --> 01:07:23,342
Focus.

1772
01:07:25,982 --> 01:07:29,022
(Getting back to the practice after putting on glasses to focus)

1773
01:07:29,852 --> 01:07:31,752
- It's good. - Yes, it's good.

1774
01:07:32,082 --> 01:07:33,192
I can do it.

1775
01:07:34,352 --> 01:07:35,492
Good luck.

1776
01:07:36,062 --> 01:07:37,692
(She presses her lips to focus.)

1777
01:07:38,162 --> 01:07:39,361
(She faces the left-turn section.)

1778
01:07:39,362 --> 01:07:41,691
- Turn. - Turn more.

1779
01:07:41,692 --> 01:07:42,702
(Halting)

1780
01:07:43,262 --> 01:07:45,161
- You need to go really slowly. - That's right.

1781
01:07:45,162 --> 01:07:46,502
She made it.

1782
01:07:48,602 --> 01:07:50,671
It looks like she's used to it now.

1783
01:07:50,672 --> 01:07:52,171
Parking is the most difficult,

1784
01:07:52,172 --> 01:07:53,672
but it looks like she'll pass at this rate.

1785
01:07:54,172 --> 01:07:55,882
Excuse me, can I try this one more time?

1786
01:07:58,242 --> 01:07:59,482
Well done.

1787
01:07:59,582 --> 01:08:01,011
That's why you keep practicing.

1788
01:08:01,012 --> 01:08:03,251
It's because she's anxious. Just in case...

1789
01:08:03,252 --> 01:08:04,822
- That's right. - Practice is the only way.

1790
01:08:05,182 --> 01:08:06,952
Don't worry too much, and don't be too nervous.

1791
01:08:07,652 --> 01:08:10,122
The simulator is more difficult than the real one.

1792
01:08:12,562 --> 01:08:16,062
(After a long practice...)

1793
01:08:16,232 --> 01:08:17,332
Don't be nervous.

1794
01:08:17,462 --> 01:08:18,872
You can do well if you don't get nervous.

1795
01:08:19,202 --> 01:08:20,402
But I'm really nervous.

1796
01:08:21,132 --> 01:08:23,002
- Thank you. - Thank you. Great job.

1797
01:08:23,842 --> 01:08:25,911
My biggest motto is,

1798
01:08:25,912 --> 01:08:27,412
"Let's try it anyway."

1799
01:08:27,742 --> 01:08:30,942
There's nothing more important than experience.

1800
01:08:31,112 --> 01:08:32,281
So let's give it a try.

1801
01:08:32,282 --> 01:08:33,412
Let's try hard.

1802
01:08:35,012 --> 01:08:36,681
(Weeping)

1803
01:08:36,682 --> 01:08:38,022
What do I do?

1804
01:08:39,552 --> 01:08:42,462
(She heads to the test site across the road, filled with worries.)

1805
01:08:44,892 --> 01:08:45,892
(Sighing)

1806
01:08:45,892 --> 01:08:46,892
(Thinking)

1807
01:08:47,992 --> 01:08:49,762
(Standing demurely)

1808
01:08:50,602 --> 01:08:52,672
(The light changed.)

1809
01:08:53,232 --> 01:08:55,232
(Skipping)

1810
01:08:56,342 --> 01:08:58,101
She's stepping on them on purpose...

1811
01:08:58,102 --> 01:08:59,142
- because of the test. - You're right.

1812
01:08:59,212 --> 01:09:00,941
- To not jinx the test... - You're right.

1813
01:09:00,942 --> 01:09:02,012
Oh, a jinx?

1814
01:09:02,342 --> 01:09:03,811
She doesn't want to step on the line.

1815
01:09:03,812 --> 01:09:06,052
- You can't step on the line. - No, you can't.

1816
01:09:07,412 --> 01:09:09,822
(She passes the main gate without stepping on the line.)

1817
01:09:10,552 --> 01:09:12,152
(Let's see.)

1818
01:09:13,452 --> 01:09:16,222
(Here we go.)

1819
01:09:17,392 --> 01:09:19,632
(Now she's only stepping on the red bricks.)

1820
01:09:20,032 --> 01:09:21,791
- It's because of a jinx. - That's important.

1821
01:09:21,792 --> 01:09:23,561
- Seriously. - But you stepped on the blue line.

1822
01:09:23,562 --> 01:09:24,931
No, I didn't!

1823
01:09:24,932 --> 01:09:26,171
She stepped on the line on the crosswalk too.

1824
01:09:26,172 --> 01:09:27,631
- That's not true! - I saw it too.

1825
01:09:27,632 --> 01:09:28,831
- You saw it too, right? - Yes.

1826
01:09:28,832 --> 01:09:29,902
Take that back.

1827
01:09:30,342 --> 01:09:31,472
Is it here?

1828
01:09:33,712 --> 01:09:35,312
Hello.

1829
01:09:35,542 --> 01:09:36,681
What can I help you with?

1830
01:09:36,682 --> 01:09:40,112
I'm here for the practical test.

1831
01:09:41,382 --> 01:09:42,722
Please give me your ID.

1832
01:09:43,352 --> 01:09:44,452
Here you go.

1833
01:09:45,152 --> 01:09:48,522
Please go to the building on the right outside.

1834
01:09:49,192 --> 01:09:50,862
- Thank you. - Goodbye.

1835
01:09:51,622 --> 01:09:53,932
(Entering the test site with the application form in her arms)

1836
01:09:54,932 --> 01:09:57,602
Is that it? Is that the truck I'm going to be driving?

1837
01:09:58,402 --> 01:10:00,972
(The truck for the test caught Jung's eyes.)

1838
01:10:02,572 --> 01:10:03,771
You're getting on the truck...

1839
01:10:03,772 --> 01:10:04,942
- for the first time? - That's right.

1840
01:10:06,342 --> 01:10:07,372
(Surprised)

1841
01:10:07,712 --> 01:10:09,442
I think it's this course.

1842
01:10:11,312 --> 01:10:12,451
Yes, that's the one.

1843
01:10:12,452 --> 01:10:14,282
Gosh, it was overwhelming.

1844
01:10:14,682 --> 01:10:16,951
(The tests are actually being held.)

1845
01:10:16,952 --> 01:10:18,181
You need to get a good car too.

1846
01:10:18,182 --> 01:10:19,992
- If you get a weird one... - That's right.

1847
01:10:21,352 --> 01:10:23,022
(It's more nerve-racking to see it in person.)

1848
01:10:23,222 --> 01:10:25,062
(Sniffling)

1849
01:10:27,332 --> 01:10:29,132
Hello.

1850
01:10:30,362 --> 01:10:32,732
(To the quiet waiting room for the practical test)

1851
01:10:35,632 --> 01:10:37,571
- You always wait there... - That's right.

1852
01:10:37,572 --> 01:10:38,742
and watch others taking the test.

1853
01:10:38,842 --> 01:10:39,972
(Hitting)

1854
01:10:44,882 --> 01:10:48,082
Jung is really brave, though.

1855
01:10:48,282 --> 01:10:49,651
You need to try getting in the car.

1856
01:10:49,652 --> 01:10:53,051
Right? To take the test without getting in the car before...

1857
01:10:53,052 --> 01:10:55,122
But I asked around,

1858
01:10:55,352 --> 01:10:57,561
- and they all said... Yes. - They did what you did?

1859
01:10:57,562 --> 01:10:58,821
They gave it a try...

1860
01:10:58,822 --> 01:11:00,092
- without trying a real car. - Yes, that's possible.

1861
01:11:00,332 --> 01:11:01,962
Their generation watches videos a lot.

1862
01:11:02,662 --> 01:11:03,801
Gosh, I'm nervous.

1863
01:11:03,802 --> 01:11:04,831
(The video-generation Jung is still nervous.)

1864
01:11:04,832 --> 01:11:05,832
(Sighing)

1865
01:11:06,602 --> 01:11:08,271
The 4pm test will begin now.

1866
01:11:08,272 --> 01:11:09,572
Ms. Lee Ji Young.

1867
01:11:11,602 --> 01:11:13,941
(They announce the start of the test.)

1868
01:11:13,942 --> 01:11:16,211
- The narration makes you nervous. - That's right.

1869
01:11:16,212 --> 01:11:19,082
- I wish she could be sweeter. - She sounds really mean.

1870
01:11:20,282 --> 01:11:22,722
(The other test takers prepare for their tests first.)

1871
01:11:23,952 --> 01:11:25,351
(There are 4 sections.)

1872
01:11:25,352 --> 01:11:27,391
(A ramp, turn,)

1873
01:11:27,392 --> 01:11:28,591
(intersection)

1874
01:11:28,592 --> 01:11:30,392
The changed test isn't easy.

1875
01:11:32,022 --> 01:11:33,562
(You can only pass if you get over 80.)

1876
01:11:34,432 --> 01:11:37,102
(The 1st test taker takes off 1st.)

1877
01:11:37,462 --> 01:11:39,072
(Here they go!)

1878
01:11:39,772 --> 01:11:42,171
Even though they were strangers, I couldn't help but root for them.

1879
01:11:42,172 --> 01:11:43,802
- That's right. - They were complete strangers.

1880
01:11:45,072 --> 01:11:46,572
(Turning)

1881
01:11:50,142 --> 01:11:52,582
(She practices in the air out of desperation.)

1882
01:11:52,912 --> 01:11:56,452
Car number 29. It stepped on the parking line number 4.

1883
01:11:57,852 --> 01:11:59,551
- You can't step on the line. - When you see that,

1884
01:11:59,552 --> 01:12:00,652
you'll be mentally out of it.

1885
01:12:00,922 --> 01:12:02,561
(The test is being broadcast in real time.)

1886
01:12:02,562 --> 01:12:05,222
Car number 23 is disqualified.

1887
01:12:05,322 --> 01:12:06,661
If the test takers before you get disqualified,

1888
01:12:06,662 --> 01:12:07,962
it drives you crazy.

1889
01:12:08,662 --> 01:12:10,361
(Disqualified as soon as it started)

1890
01:12:10,362 --> 01:12:12,162
It got disqualified as soon as it started?

1891
01:12:12,232 --> 01:12:14,302
You get disqualified if you start without releasing the handbrake.

1892
01:12:15,302 --> 01:12:16,871
They started without releasing the handbrake?

1893
01:12:16,872 --> 01:12:19,311
Yes, but there are quite a lot of people who make such mistakes.

1894
01:12:19,312 --> 01:12:20,542
- I did. - That's right.

1895
01:12:20,712 --> 01:12:22,371
Well, I didn't release...

1896
01:12:22,372 --> 01:12:23,681
The handbrake?

1897
01:12:23,682 --> 01:12:25,381
Yes, so I got disqualified right away.

1898
01:12:25,382 --> 01:12:27,451
Actually, the pass rate of the practical test...

1899
01:12:27,452 --> 01:12:29,681
- is only about 30 percent. - Really?

1900
01:12:29,682 --> 01:12:31,521
Because you're nervous, you forget what you already know.

1901
01:12:31,522 --> 01:12:34,051
Yes, you forget what you're always aware of.

1902
01:12:34,052 --> 01:12:35,492
- That's right. - That's right.

1903
01:12:36,362 --> 01:12:39,792
Car number 18. It stepped on the parking line number 2.

1904
01:12:40,462 --> 01:12:42,501
Car number 13 is disqualified.

1905
01:12:42,502 --> 01:12:43,661
It sounds like the voice from "Squid Game."

1906
01:12:43,662 --> 01:12:45,702
- It does sound like "Squid Game." - Exactly.

1907
01:12:45,902 --> 01:12:46,932
It's disqualified.

1908
01:12:47,002 --> 01:12:49,072
(The test takers get disqualified in a row.)

1909
01:12:49,742 --> 01:12:52,642
Car number 18. It's disqualified on the ramp.

1910
01:12:53,242 --> 01:12:54,711
(Switching the driver as they're disqualified)

1911
01:12:54,712 --> 01:12:57,281
- It's really embarrassing then. - I know.

1912
01:12:57,282 --> 01:12:59,652
The test taker was dragged out like GTA.

1913
01:13:00,912 --> 01:13:03,251
Car number 29. Congratulations.

1914
01:13:03,252 --> 01:13:04,822
- You passed. - That was the first person to pass.

1915
01:13:05,522 --> 01:13:06,592
Good for them.

1916
01:13:06,922 --> 01:13:09,161
Car number 30. Congratulations.

1917
01:13:09,162 --> 01:13:10,392
(Envious)

1918
01:13:11,062 --> 01:13:14,692
(The rest of them are being called one by one.)

1919
01:13:15,262 --> 01:13:16,802
(The waiting room starts to get empty.)

1920
01:13:17,402 --> 01:13:18,532
When will my turn come?

1921
01:13:19,932 --> 01:13:21,972
(Jung is the only one left in the waiting room.)

1922
01:13:22,232 --> 01:13:23,371
Am I the last one?

1923
01:13:23,372 --> 01:13:24,842
(Am I the last to go?)

1924
01:13:25,702 --> 01:13:27,412
(Shaking)

1925
01:13:28,712 --> 01:13:30,312
Gosh, what's with the cloud?

1926
01:13:31,112 --> 01:13:32,552
Oh, no. A crow.

1927
01:13:33,982 --> 01:13:36,122
(Anxious)

1928
01:13:38,422 --> 01:13:40,091
My stomach hurts because I'm nervous.

1929
01:13:40,092 --> 01:13:41,592
That's right.

1930
01:13:41,652 --> 01:13:43,121
That's why you need to use the restroom before.

1931
01:13:43,122 --> 01:13:44,722
- You must go. - For real.

1932
01:13:47,232 --> 01:13:49,632
Ms. Lee Jung.

1933
01:13:50,862 --> 01:13:52,431
(It's finally my turn.)

1934
01:13:52,432 --> 01:13:53,672
She's doing it now.

1935
01:13:54,172 --> 01:13:55,231
(After identity verification...)

1936
01:13:55,232 --> 01:13:56,541
Get in car number three.

1937
01:13:56,542 --> 01:13:57,601
Car number three.

1938
01:13:57,602 --> 01:13:59,972
(I'm nervous.)

1939
01:14:00,212 --> 01:14:01,541
- Ms. Lee Jung. - Yes.

1940
01:14:01,542 --> 01:14:02,742
Please come this way.

1941
01:14:03,612 --> 01:14:05,081
That's when your hands start to get cold.

1942
01:14:05,082 --> 01:14:06,512
Yes, and they shake too.

1943
01:14:07,573 --> 01:14:10,213
(She heads to the truck for the test with clenched fists.)

1944
01:14:14,713 --> 01:14:15,783
Thank you.

1945
01:14:16,223 --> 01:14:17,252
Yes.

1946
01:14:17,253 --> 01:14:19,193
(Let's not forget the seatbelt.)

1947
01:14:20,023 --> 01:14:21,253
You can do it.

1948
01:14:22,023 --> 01:14:24,223
- Follow the instructions relaxedly. - Okay.

1949
01:14:25,193 --> 01:14:27,792
It's here, and this is here.

1950
01:14:27,793 --> 01:14:29,403
(Quickly scanning the inside)

1951
01:14:29,563 --> 01:14:30,933
- We'll begin. - All right.

1952
01:14:31,333 --> 01:14:34,203
Car number three. Ms. Lee Jung is ready.

1953
01:14:36,003 --> 01:14:38,242
- Good luck. - "Good luck."

1954
01:14:38,243 --> 01:14:39,272
Stay calm.

1955
01:14:39,273 --> 01:14:40,273
(Sighing)

1956
01:14:41,173 --> 01:14:42,183
(Sighing)

1957
01:14:43,143 --> 01:14:44,512
(Shaking)

1958
01:14:44,513 --> 01:14:46,412
- Don't shake your legs. - It was real.

1959
01:14:46,413 --> 01:14:47,852
- Don't shake your legs! - Why are you shaking so much?

1960
01:14:47,853 --> 01:14:49,722
- That was... I was seriously... - Hold on.

1961
01:14:49,723 --> 01:14:51,023
- I... - She lost all her good luck.

1962
01:14:51,083 --> 01:14:53,122
I was really nervous that I...

1963
01:14:53,123 --> 01:14:54,692
- I get it, but... - That'd drive your fortune out.

1964
01:14:54,693 --> 01:14:56,022
You lost all your good luck.

1965
01:14:56,023 --> 01:14:57,863
But what was I supposed to do? I was so nervous.

1966
01:14:58,963 --> 01:15:01,733
(Barely holding on to her trembling heart)

1967
01:15:02,703 --> 01:15:04,532
(Into the world of driving)

1968
01:15:04,533 --> 01:15:06,872
The test will begin for car number three.

1969
01:15:06,873 --> 01:15:08,473
I was really nervous.

1970
01:15:09,703 --> 01:15:10,743
(Sighing)

1971
01:15:11,503 --> 01:15:13,542
- This is nothing. - We will begin the test.

1972
01:15:13,543 --> 01:15:15,412
- It's nothing. - Your points might get deducted...

1973
01:15:15,413 --> 01:15:17,643
if you use any parts different from the instruction,

1974
01:15:17,743 --> 01:15:19,053
so please keep that in mind.

1975
01:15:19,713 --> 01:15:21,583
Why can't I stay still?

1976
01:15:21,613 --> 01:15:23,853
We will begin the test now.

1977
01:15:24,423 --> 01:15:26,993
Start the engine within five seconds.

1978
01:15:27,953 --> 01:15:29,692
(The test begins with operating the drive controls.)

1979
01:15:29,693 --> 01:15:31,193
(Clicking)

1980
01:15:32,693 --> 01:15:34,293
We will begin the test now.

1981
01:15:35,063 --> 01:15:38,532
Turn on the left turn signal within five seconds.

1982
01:15:38,533 --> 01:15:40,333
It's really nerve-racking that there are only five seconds.

1983
01:15:41,233 --> 01:15:44,443
Turn off the turn signal within five seconds.

1984
01:15:45,743 --> 01:15:47,743
Some people turn on the wipers by mistake.

1985
01:15:48,273 --> 01:15:50,343
- Oh, not the turn signals? - Oh, right. The wipers.

1986
01:15:51,113 --> 01:15:53,752
Shift the gear lever to neutral, then switch it back...

1987
01:15:53,753 --> 01:15:55,452
- to the parking position... - There were such tests.

1988
01:15:55,453 --> 01:15:56,482
- within ten seconds. - I totally forgot.

1989
01:15:56,483 --> 01:15:57,883
Shift to N and then to P.

1990
01:15:58,823 --> 01:16:00,692
(Jung calmly does what she's learned.)

1991
01:16:00,693 --> 01:16:01,723
(Exhaling)

1992
01:16:05,193 --> 01:16:07,093
Watching that makes me nervous again.

1993
01:16:07,933 --> 01:16:11,433
Now, we will test your basic driving ability.

1994
01:16:11,663 --> 01:16:13,533
We will begin now.

1995
01:16:13,733 --> 01:16:14,733
- Break a leg. - Good luck.

1996
01:16:14,734 --> 01:16:17,073
Release the brake and start.

1997
01:16:19,573 --> 01:16:20,772
She released the handbrake.

1998
01:16:20,773 --> 01:16:22,012
(Exhaling)

1999
01:16:22,013 --> 01:16:23,082
That's it.

2000
01:16:23,083 --> 01:16:25,352
Why am I breathing so hard?

2001
01:16:25,353 --> 01:16:27,383
You're really calm comparatively.

2002
01:16:28,683 --> 01:16:30,182
(She sets off without deducting any points.)

2003
01:16:30,183 --> 01:16:31,483
That was good.

2004
01:16:32,623 --> 01:16:34,293
This is nothing.

2005
01:16:35,723 --> 01:16:37,393
Jung, it's okay even if you fail.

2006
01:16:37,763 --> 01:16:39,833
Just try hard and do your best.

2007
01:16:39,993 --> 01:16:42,463
Focus, all right?

2008
01:16:42,863 --> 01:16:44,202
I did that too. I talked to myself.

2009
01:16:44,203 --> 01:16:45,833
You tend to speak to yourself a lot.

2010
01:16:47,873 --> 01:16:49,843
I've never seen you getting this nervous.

2011
01:16:50,103 --> 01:16:52,673
It's been so long since I got that nervous too.

2012
01:16:53,843 --> 01:16:55,642
(She's arrived at the ramp, the second section.)

2013
01:16:55,643 --> 01:16:57,142
- Stop. - This part is important.

2014
01:16:57,143 --> 01:16:59,483
- Oh, don't cross the line. - The line.

2015
01:16:59,713 --> 01:17:01,953
- Do it calmly. Step on the brake. - The line. Good job.

2016
01:17:02,323 --> 01:17:03,852
So far, she's doing well.

2017
01:17:03,853 --> 01:17:05,123
You're doing well.

2018
01:17:05,653 --> 01:17:07,693
(Wait for 3 seconds.)

2019
01:17:09,523 --> 01:17:11,723
(She goes after keeping the time.)

2020
01:17:12,093 --> 01:17:14,833
That's good. You're doing well.

2021
01:17:14,933 --> 01:17:16,263
Drive slowly.

2022
01:17:16,663 --> 01:17:18,603
There you go. Drive slowly.

2023
01:17:18,903 --> 01:17:20,973
There you go. Go slowly.

2024
01:17:21,273 --> 01:17:22,503
Focus.

2025
01:17:22,843 --> 01:17:25,542
There you go. Be careful here...

2026
01:17:25,543 --> 01:17:27,343
because you're turning left here.

2027
01:17:28,573 --> 01:17:30,012
- This part. - Gosh, this part.

2028
01:17:30,013 --> 01:17:31,843
- All right. Turn the wheel. - Go slowly.

2029
01:17:32,653 --> 01:17:33,882
(The corner turning section wasn't easy during practice also.)

2030
01:17:33,883 --> 01:17:35,382
You'll get disqualified for sure if you bump into that.

2031
01:17:35,383 --> 01:17:37,082
Your points don't get deducted. You get disqualified right away.

2032
01:17:37,083 --> 01:17:38,583
(This is too hard.)

2033
01:17:39,593 --> 01:17:40,623
From here...

2034
01:17:41,723 --> 01:17:43,123
Stay calm.

2035
01:17:44,563 --> 01:17:47,433
(Even I'm more nervous.)

2036
01:17:48,593 --> 01:17:50,003
(Sweating profusely)

2037
01:17:50,463 --> 01:17:53,173
- Good. - Yes. I think it's good.

2038
01:17:53,473 --> 01:17:55,743
There you go. You did well.

2039
01:17:57,473 --> 01:18:00,072
- You're doing well. - You did well.

2040
01:18:00,073 --> 01:18:01,512
Go slowly.

2041
01:18:01,513 --> 01:18:02,913
Turn left here.

2042
01:18:03,643 --> 01:18:04,843
Turn now.

2043
01:18:04,913 --> 01:18:06,152
Gosh, this is so stressful.

2044
01:18:06,153 --> 01:18:07,153
(Turning the wheel breathlessly)

2045
01:18:07,253 --> 01:18:10,422
There you go! You're doing well.

2046
01:18:10,423 --> 01:18:11,552
(Please...)

2047
01:18:11,553 --> 01:18:13,522
There you go. That's good.

2048
01:18:13,523 --> 01:18:14,753
(She passes the next left-turn section as well!)

2049
01:18:15,563 --> 01:18:18,293
- You're doing well. - Shall I check? So far, so good.

2050
01:18:18,493 --> 01:18:20,263
It was smoother than I thought.

2051
01:18:20,433 --> 01:18:22,333
I saw how my points didn't get deducted at all,

2052
01:18:23,103 --> 01:18:24,133
so I thought I was a genius.

2053
01:18:25,203 --> 01:18:26,803
(Amazed)

2054
01:18:27,773 --> 01:18:30,042
(Maybe I'm a genius who's good at real games.)

2055
01:18:30,043 --> 01:18:31,242
It was a lot easier, right?

2056
01:18:31,243 --> 01:18:32,772
- It was rather easier... - That's right.

2057
01:18:32,773 --> 01:18:34,012
than the stimulator.

2058
01:18:34,013 --> 01:18:36,142
It's red light, so step on the brake.

2059
01:18:36,143 --> 01:18:38,442
- Oh, I can go now. - You're doing well.

2060
01:18:38,443 --> 01:18:40,113
Go a bit further from here.

2061
01:18:40,413 --> 01:18:41,652
Why am I shaking so much?

2062
01:18:41,653 --> 01:18:42,822
You're dancing with your foot.

2063
01:18:42,823 --> 01:18:44,082
(Holding on to her trembling body and driving slowly)

2064
01:18:44,083 --> 01:18:45,223
(Squirming)

2065
01:18:46,893 --> 01:18:47,953
It's parking.

2066
01:18:48,053 --> 01:18:49,263
You're good at parking.

2067
01:18:49,323 --> 01:18:50,563
I'm confident in parking.

2068
01:18:50,823 --> 01:18:52,633
Where should I park?

2069
01:18:52,663 --> 01:18:54,693
- Go to number one. - Oh, thank you.

2070
01:18:54,963 --> 01:18:57,032
What was I to do from here? All right. Let's see.

2071
01:18:57,033 --> 01:18:59,773
Position the car in line with your shoulder. That's it.

2072
01:19:00,073 --> 01:19:01,532
- Oh, no. Your shoulder. - Oh, dear.

2073
01:19:01,533 --> 01:19:02,772
- It's okay. - Oh, no.

2074
01:19:02,773 --> 01:19:04,503
Go slowly. There you go.

2075
01:19:04,603 --> 01:19:05,772
You're stepping on the brake too much.

2076
01:19:05,773 --> 01:19:07,172
Because I stepped on it too hard,

2077
01:19:07,173 --> 01:19:08,712
my butt hurt so much.

2078
01:19:08,713 --> 01:19:10,742
When your butt doesn't hurt from dancing so much?

2079
01:19:10,743 --> 01:19:11,743
Seriously, my butt hurt a lot.

2080
01:19:11,744 --> 01:19:13,682
- You stepped on it too hard. - Yes.

2081
01:19:13,683 --> 01:19:15,082
If someone were in the passenger seat, they'd have thrown up.

2082
01:19:15,083 --> 01:19:16,152
That's for sure.

2083
01:19:16,153 --> 01:19:17,183
(Gagging)

2084
01:19:18,153 --> 01:19:20,823
All right. Turn it all the way.

2085
01:19:21,123 --> 01:19:23,823
(Rushed)

2086
01:19:24,223 --> 01:19:25,263
Let's go.

2087
01:19:27,363 --> 01:19:29,002
There you go. You're doing well.

2088
01:19:29,003 --> 01:19:30,903
- You did well. - She entered the section.

2089
01:19:32,203 --> 01:19:33,802
Turn it only half way, and where do I go?

2090
01:19:33,803 --> 01:19:35,133
You need to check that.

2091
01:19:35,303 --> 01:19:37,603
- There you go. Go slowly. - That's it.

2092
01:19:37,773 --> 01:19:39,343
You're doing well.

2093
01:19:41,213 --> 01:19:42,483
Gosh, is this right?

2094
01:19:42,613 --> 01:19:43,643
I have no idea.

2095
01:19:43,943 --> 01:19:45,043
(Exhaling)

2096
01:19:45,853 --> 01:19:47,082
(Even her cheek is shaking.)

2097
01:19:47,083 --> 01:19:49,082
- She's so nervous. - Oh, no.

2098
01:19:49,083 --> 01:19:50,682
- Slow down! - It's like...

2099
01:19:50,683 --> 01:19:53,253
It's like she's defusing a time bomb.

2100
01:19:54,693 --> 01:19:56,822
- It's because we know how it feels. - That's right.

2101
01:19:56,823 --> 01:19:59,193
- You get it, right? - I hate it.

2102
01:19:59,293 --> 01:20:01,063
You're not talking to someone in the back, are you?

2103
01:20:01,993 --> 01:20:03,133
"Is this right?"

2104
01:20:03,503 --> 01:20:04,903
Like I'm talking to a friend. "Is this right?"

2105
01:20:06,003 --> 01:20:08,573
(Getting ready to park while talking to herself)

2106
01:20:09,443 --> 01:20:12,073
Reverse. Now, back up slowly.

2107
01:20:13,213 --> 01:20:14,472
(Turning)

2108
01:20:14,473 --> 01:20:15,643
She's doing well.

2109
01:20:18,183 --> 01:20:20,183
- Look at her face. - Stay calm.

2110
01:20:22,213 --> 01:20:23,452
She did well.

2111
01:20:23,453 --> 01:20:24,722
(She pushes the tail in without hesitating.)

2112
01:20:24,723 --> 01:20:25,723
(Rocking)

2113
01:20:25,724 --> 01:20:27,152
You're doing well.

2114
01:20:27,153 --> 01:20:28,293
(Look how charismatic she is.)

2115
01:20:29,593 --> 01:20:30,993
Hey, slow down.

2116
01:20:31,063 --> 01:20:32,263
"Is this right?"

2117
01:20:32,963 --> 01:20:35,293
She steps on the brake really aggressively.

2118
01:20:35,393 --> 01:20:37,103
Because she doesn't have a sense for it yet.

2119
01:20:38,033 --> 01:20:39,103
Release it all the way.

2120
01:20:39,303 --> 01:20:40,933
- Oh, no. There you go. - Release it all the way.

2121
01:20:41,833 --> 01:20:44,172
Release it all the way. Back up straight.

2122
01:20:44,173 --> 01:20:45,872
- Yes, back up after releasing. - Back up straight.

2123
01:20:45,873 --> 01:20:47,273
- All right. You did it. - Go slowly.

2124
01:20:47,413 --> 01:20:49,113
- It's approved. - All right.

2125
01:20:50,013 --> 01:20:51,882
(She managed to park without deducting points.)

2126
01:20:51,883 --> 01:20:53,153
You did well.

2127
01:20:53,413 --> 01:20:54,553
Gosh, thank you.

2128
01:20:54,913 --> 01:20:56,023
(That's amazing.)

2129
01:20:56,553 --> 01:20:57,982
(Watch...)

2130
01:20:57,983 --> 01:20:59,753
(the parking skill of a genius.)

2131
01:20:59,923 --> 01:21:03,523
Release the handbrake and shift to D.

2132
01:21:04,263 --> 01:21:05,462
The shoulder line.

2133
01:21:05,463 --> 01:21:06,832
Align the car to the shoulder line.

2134
01:21:06,833 --> 01:21:08,162
- Then move out. - That's it. It's here.

2135
01:21:08,163 --> 01:21:10,232
- It's here. There you go. - There you go.

2136
01:21:10,233 --> 01:21:11,663
"Is your shoulder line here?"

2137
01:21:12,533 --> 01:21:14,203
Gosh, that's totally...

2138
01:21:14,973 --> 01:21:17,142
(Let's go to the next course!)

2139
01:21:17,143 --> 01:21:18,772
Your points are deducted for stepping on the line.

2140
01:21:18,773 --> 01:21:20,072
No!

2141
01:21:20,073 --> 01:21:21,512
Your points are deducted for stepping on the line.

2142
01:21:21,513 --> 01:21:22,643
Gosh, what is this?

2143
01:21:22,683 --> 01:21:24,043
(Shocked)

2144
01:21:24,683 --> 01:21:26,052
(No, please...)

2145
01:21:26,053 --> 01:21:27,382
You should watch as you go.

2146
01:21:27,383 --> 01:21:28,652
All right. It's okay.

2147
01:21:28,653 --> 01:21:30,953
It's okay. Just give up. It's all right.

2148
01:21:31,523 --> 01:21:32,722
It doesn't matter.

2149
01:21:32,723 --> 01:21:34,492
Right. You didn't have any points deducted.

2150
01:21:34,493 --> 01:21:35,692
- I just need to keep going. - Just go.

2151
01:21:35,693 --> 01:21:37,393
- Your points are deducted. - What's wrong?

2152
01:21:37,693 --> 01:21:38,693
Your points are deducted for stepping on the line.

2153
01:21:38,694 --> 01:21:39,762
You can't go back and forth.

2154
01:21:39,763 --> 01:21:41,332
- No. Just go. - Just hurry up and go.

2155
01:21:41,333 --> 01:21:42,662
If you go back and forth here, your points...

2156
01:21:42,663 --> 01:21:43,932
- will keep getting deducted. - Just go!

2157
01:21:43,933 --> 01:21:46,433
(Everyone is coaching her desperately.)

2158
01:21:47,103 --> 01:21:48,172
(It's frustrating for her even now.)

2159
01:21:48,173 --> 01:21:49,972
- You should just hurry and leave. - You should just leave.

2160
01:21:49,973 --> 01:21:51,043
Run away.

2161
01:21:52,613 --> 01:21:53,613
No.

2162
01:21:54,073 --> 01:21:55,982
I can't lose any more points now.

2163
01:21:55,983 --> 01:21:57,813
If you make one more mistake, you'll be disqualified?

2164
01:21:57,983 --> 01:21:59,713
Hold on, Jung. Calm down.

2165
01:22:00,053 --> 01:22:01,253
Let's back up a bit.

2166
01:22:01,553 --> 01:22:02,882
- Back up? - Why would you back up?

2167
01:22:02,883 --> 01:22:03,883
- No! - Don't back up!

2168
01:22:03,884 --> 01:22:05,152
Why would you back up?

2169
01:22:05,153 --> 01:22:06,323
No, let's just go.

2170
01:22:07,493 --> 01:22:09,123
- Go forward. - Go forward.

2171
01:22:09,523 --> 01:22:11,023
That's right.

2172
01:22:12,593 --> 01:22:13,732
(Shaking)

2173
01:22:13,733 --> 01:22:14,833
What's wrong?

2174
01:22:15,563 --> 01:22:16,962
- What's wrong? - Because she's scared,

2175
01:22:16,963 --> 01:22:18,003
she stepped on the brake.

2176
01:22:18,433 --> 01:22:20,073
What's wrong? What are you doing?

2177
01:22:21,373 --> 01:22:23,443
(The car went up onto the curb.)

2178
01:22:24,903 --> 01:22:26,413
You're disqualified by authority.

2179
01:22:28,213 --> 01:22:31,042
(A bolt out of the blue)

2180
01:22:31,043 --> 01:22:33,313
No!

2181
01:22:33,913 --> 01:22:35,952
- Bye. - Bye.

2182
01:22:35,953 --> 01:22:37,622
- But seriously... - You're disqualified, right?

2183
01:22:37,623 --> 01:22:39,252
See you again.

2184
01:22:39,253 --> 01:22:41,622
- What was that about? - I mean... I...

2185
01:22:41,623 --> 01:22:43,192
You passed all the difficult parts.

2186
01:22:43,193 --> 01:22:45,262
I was so dumbfounded too.

2187
01:22:45,263 --> 01:22:48,932
But once you get your points deducted in a row...

2188
01:22:48,933 --> 01:22:50,933
- That's when you lose your cool. - Right. You'd lose your cool.

2189
01:22:50,963 --> 01:22:52,002
You just lost your cool.

2190
01:22:52,003 --> 01:22:53,933
I really thought I was in "Squid Game."

2191
01:22:54,073 --> 01:22:55,572
You could've gotten 4.56 million dollars.

2192
01:22:55,573 --> 01:22:56,942
You died at the end.

2193
01:22:56,943 --> 01:22:58,442
- I thought she'd pass. - Me too.

2194
01:22:58,443 --> 01:22:59,713
- It's a bummer. - Naturally.

2195
01:22:59,813 --> 01:23:03,482
Wouldn't you have passed if you just crossed the finish line?

2196
01:23:03,483 --> 01:23:05,542
- I had to pass the intersection... - Right?

2197
01:23:05,543 --> 01:23:07,282
and speed up.

2198
01:23:07,283 --> 01:23:08,482
Oh, you have to drive fast at the end?

2199
01:23:08,483 --> 01:23:10,122
- The speeding section. - Right. There's that too.

2200
01:23:10,123 --> 01:23:11,422
- Speeding is easy. - Right.

2201
01:23:11,423 --> 01:23:12,623
That was close.

2202
01:23:13,793 --> 01:23:16,063
(She was disqualified by authority when she almost made it.)

2203
01:23:16,723 --> 01:23:19,262
(I can't believe it ended like this.)

2204
01:23:19,263 --> 01:23:20,433
That was close.

2205
01:23:22,463 --> 01:23:24,862
(Why do I keep tearing up like this?)

2206
01:23:24,863 --> 01:23:26,673
You'd tear up then.

2207
01:23:26,733 --> 01:23:28,003
Let me take over.

2208
01:23:30,543 --> 01:23:31,673
Thank you.

2209
01:23:32,543 --> 01:23:33,573
Please get out.

2210
01:23:34,143 --> 01:23:35,312
"Please get out."

2211
01:23:35,313 --> 01:23:36,942
- Thank you. - They drag you out so meanly.

2212
01:23:36,943 --> 01:23:38,713
- Like GTA. - Sit in the back.

2213
01:23:39,253 --> 01:23:40,553
- In the back? - Yes.

2214
01:23:40,783 --> 01:23:41,812
Thank you.

2215
01:23:41,813 --> 01:23:44,383
(Exiled to the backseat)

2216
01:23:45,153 --> 01:23:46,192
(Crying)

2217
01:23:46,193 --> 01:23:47,723
(Ending the test, leaving regrets behind)

2218
01:23:48,623 --> 01:23:50,993
(I'm an 8t truck with a broken wheel)

2219
01:23:51,563 --> 01:23:54,063
(She parked well but went the wrong way.)

2220
01:23:57,733 --> 01:24:00,132
(A wheel turning mistake too late to undo)

2221
01:24:00,133 --> 01:24:01,573
(Crying)

2222
01:24:03,203 --> 01:24:05,343
(I want to go back.)

2223
01:24:05,373 --> 01:24:07,812
You get to go on a drive. Sitting at the back looks cool.

2224
01:24:07,813 --> 01:24:08,913
You look like a rich lady.

2225
01:24:09,943 --> 01:24:11,213
But I failed the test.

2226
01:24:11,913 --> 01:24:12,982
- Thank you. - Go to the second floor.

2227
01:24:12,983 --> 01:24:14,012
- The second floor? - Yes.

2228
01:24:14,013 --> 01:24:15,813
That's the most embarrassing moment.

2229
01:24:16,123 --> 01:24:17,352
It's the most embarrassing for real.

2230
01:24:17,353 --> 01:24:19,593
- I've never been that embarrassed. - Thank you.

2231
01:24:21,353 --> 01:24:22,392
(Hitting)

2232
01:24:22,393 --> 01:24:23,822
Oh, dear.

2233
01:24:23,823 --> 01:24:25,362
(Stumbling)

2234
01:24:25,363 --> 01:24:26,463
I hit it too hard.

2235
01:24:27,763 --> 01:24:28,832
(She just laughs, forgetting the pain.)

2236
01:24:28,833 --> 01:24:29,833
No...

2237
01:24:30,263 --> 01:24:31,402
What did I do wrong?

2238
01:24:31,403 --> 01:24:32,703
If I reversed...

2239
01:24:32,903 --> 01:24:34,803
I should've turned this way and gone that way.

2240
01:24:37,143 --> 01:24:38,143
(Sighing)

2241
01:24:38,144 --> 01:24:39,242
She passed all the difficult sections.

2242
01:24:39,243 --> 01:24:40,972
- I know. - You're right. She did.

2243
01:24:40,973 --> 01:24:42,112
- It's a bummer. - She should've failed...

2244
01:24:42,113 --> 01:24:43,383
- in the beginning. - That's right.

2245
01:24:46,453 --> 01:24:47,512
(It's not easy to get a driver's license.)

2246
01:24:47,513 --> 01:24:48,712
She'll pass next time.

2247
01:24:48,713 --> 01:24:49,823
You're right.

2248
01:24:50,483 --> 01:24:52,023
Gosh, I'm so tired.

2249
01:24:54,853 --> 01:24:56,663
That was really close.

2250
01:24:57,623 --> 01:24:59,463
I have to go and get "fail" stamped.

2251
01:24:59,563 --> 01:25:01,032
- It's already sad... - Hello.

2252
01:25:01,033 --> 01:25:02,262
- That's a bit... - that she failed.

2253
01:25:02,263 --> 01:25:03,332
- And she has to get that too? - Oh, right.

2254
01:25:03,333 --> 01:25:04,802
You can come back again.

2255
01:25:04,803 --> 01:25:07,133
Thank you. Goodbye.

2256
01:25:07,303 --> 01:25:09,033
- She got the mark for "fail." - How embarrassing.

2257
01:25:09,343 --> 01:25:10,572
It was humiliating.

2258
01:25:10,573 --> 01:25:11,943
(Looking for somewhere to hide)

2259
01:25:13,543 --> 01:25:14,673
How futile.

2260
01:25:16,113 --> 01:25:17,282
(Crying)

2261
01:25:17,283 --> 01:25:18,582
When can you retake the test?

2262
01:25:18,583 --> 01:25:20,582
After failing,

2263
01:25:20,583 --> 01:25:23,053
you need to wait three days to give it a try again.

2264
01:25:24,023 --> 01:25:25,653
(She comes outside looking down.)

2265
01:25:27,093 --> 01:25:28,723
The weather was especially nice.

2266
01:25:29,423 --> 01:25:30,562
(Jung calls someone.)

2267
01:25:30,563 --> 01:25:32,322
(Who could it be?)

2268
01:25:32,323 --> 01:25:34,033
- Hello. - Dad.

2269
01:25:34,333 --> 01:25:35,392
Yes.

2270
01:25:35,393 --> 01:25:37,863
I just took the practical test, and I failed.

2271
01:25:38,103 --> 01:25:39,433
- You failed? - Yes.

2272
01:25:39,903 --> 01:25:42,073
(She whines to her dad as she's disappointed.)

2273
01:25:42,203 --> 01:25:44,243
There are two ways.

2274
01:25:44,503 --> 01:25:45,842
Getting a license no matter what...

2275
01:25:45,843 --> 01:25:47,712
and driving yourself.

2276
01:25:47,713 --> 01:25:48,713
Yes.

2277
01:25:48,714 --> 01:25:50,282
Or cutting off driving in your life...

2278
01:25:50,283 --> 01:25:51,882
and not driving could be another way.

2279
01:25:51,883 --> 01:25:53,012
- That's a solution too. - Of course.

2280
01:25:53,013 --> 01:25:54,083
You're right.

2281
01:25:54,853 --> 01:25:58,482
But even if I don't drive, I must get the Type One license.

2282
01:25:58,483 --> 01:26:00,122
It's really firing me up.

2283
01:26:00,123 --> 01:26:02,293
- Right. It fires you up. - Yes, it does.

2284
01:26:02,923 --> 01:26:04,892
Sure. Go ahead and try. You can get it.

2285
01:26:04,893 --> 01:26:07,163
- All right, Dad. - All right.

2286
01:26:07,793 --> 01:26:10,402
I felt really grateful for everyone...

2287
01:26:10,403 --> 01:26:12,233
who drives for me.

2288
01:26:12,433 --> 01:26:13,832
First of all, there's my mom and dad.

2289
01:26:13,833 --> 01:26:15,532
And Yoon Seo who sometimes picks me up...

2290
01:26:15,533 --> 01:26:17,773
or drives me home.

2291
01:26:17,873 --> 01:26:22,242
And the taxi drivers and bus drivers who always drive for me.

2292
01:26:22,243 --> 01:26:25,643
I have huge respect for everyone on the road...

2293
01:26:26,253 --> 01:26:27,812
- who drives safely. - Yes, you feel love for humankind.

2294
01:26:27,813 --> 01:26:28,813
That's right.

2295
01:26:28,814 --> 01:26:31,322
- I'll call you again. - All right.

2296
01:26:31,323 --> 01:26:33,122
- Okay, rest well. - Okay.

2297
01:26:33,123 --> 01:26:34,123
Bye.

2298
01:26:34,124 --> 01:26:35,953
(And I Will Give It a Try Again)

2299
01:26:36,093 --> 01:26:37,623
(Next story)

2300
01:26:38,593 --> 01:26:40,492
(To meet special people,)

2301
01:26:40,493 --> 01:26:42,163
(he has arrived somewhere.)

2302
01:26:43,063 --> 01:26:44,663
(Yeongcheon National Cemetery)

2303
01:26:45,333 --> 01:26:47,302
(His grandfather and grandmother...)

2304
01:26:47,303 --> 01:26:49,133
(who are people of national merit)

2305
01:26:49,503 --> 01:26:50,573
Here it is.

2306
01:26:50,673 --> 01:26:52,842
(Have you been well?)

2307
01:26:52,843 --> 01:26:53,843
(Army Sergeant First Class)

2308
01:26:54,313 --> 01:26:57,513
(The rain stopped miraculously when he was about to give a bow.)

2309
01:26:57,913 --> 01:26:59,812
(The day my grandmother passed...)

2310
01:26:59,813 --> 01:27:01,753
(was the same date as my birthday.)

2311
01:27:02,453 --> 01:27:05,053
(The past days he disregarded his birthday as he was sad)

2312
01:27:05,823 --> 01:27:07,252
(He just calmly...)

2313
01:27:07,253 --> 01:27:09,323
(spent his birthdays.)

2314
01:27:09,763 --> 01:27:11,363
(To me, family means...)

2315
01:27:12,293 --> 01:27:15,162
(the assurance that I'll have something to fall back on,)

2316
01:27:15,163 --> 01:27:16,603
(no matter what I lose.)

2317
01:27:17,033 --> 01:27:19,003
(Ki Bum, come out for lunch.)

2318
01:27:19,433 --> 01:27:21,002
(He visited his house in Daegu after a long time.)

2319
01:27:21,003 --> 01:27:22,333
(Surprised)

2320
01:27:22,603 --> 01:27:24,242
(You made it yourself? You didn't get it from the supermarket?)

2321
01:27:24,243 --> 01:27:25,243
(All of them?)

2322
01:27:25,403 --> 01:27:27,543
(I can do this much.)

2323
01:27:27,743 --> 01:27:29,583
(Beef tripe in bone soup?)

2324
01:27:30,913 --> 01:27:32,612
(The bone soup recipe they missed...)

2325
01:27:32,613 --> 01:27:34,082
(that they couldn't eat but just kept to themselves)

2326
01:27:34,083 --> 01:27:35,083
- Does it taste the same? - It's good.

2327
01:27:35,084 --> 01:27:36,653
(It tastes the same.)

2328
01:27:37,483 --> 01:27:39,993
(Always Feeling You)

2329
01:27:40,423 --> 01:27:44,093
(Ju Seung visited many wedding halls at the end of last year.)

2330
01:27:47,163 --> 01:27:50,703
(Thanks to him, his brother's wedding went well.)

2331
01:27:52,203 --> 01:27:55,533
(After the wedding, they gathered at their parents' place.)

2332
01:27:56,743 --> 01:28:00,673
(And Ga Eul, his sister-in-law who is from Vietnam)

2333
01:28:01,113 --> 01:28:02,113
They're doing something.

2334
01:28:02,114 --> 01:28:03,443
(Where did they go to with a new family member?)

2335
01:28:04,183 --> 01:28:05,242
(Let me teach you more about Korean culture...)

2336
01:28:05,243 --> 01:28:07,813
(at Korean Folk Village.)

2337
01:28:08,653 --> 01:28:09,822
(Walking cozily)

2338
01:28:09,823 --> 01:28:11,223
(Linking arms with each other)

2339
01:28:11,783 --> 01:28:13,223
(Shall I take a photo for you?)

2340
01:28:13,793 --> 01:28:15,753
(Jutographer for his sister-in-law)

2341
01:28:16,663 --> 01:28:17,892
(How should I pose? I have no idea.)

2342
01:28:17,893 --> 01:28:18,923
(Shy)

2343
01:28:20,163 --> 01:28:21,493
One, two, three.

2344
01:28:22,293 --> 01:28:26,173
(Suddenly changing in front of the camera)

2345
01:28:27,333 --> 01:28:29,072
(I'll take photos with all my heart.)

2346
01:28:29,073 --> 01:28:30,102
It's so pretty.

2347
01:28:30,103 --> 01:28:32,242
(The customer is highly satisfied.)

2348
01:28:32,243 --> 01:28:33,442
I'm different as I'm a pro.

2349
01:28:33,443 --> 01:28:34,613
(I proved myself, didn't I?)

2350
01:28:36,213 --> 01:28:37,213
(Stretching)

2351
01:28:37,783 --> 01:28:40,253
(Jutographer does his best.)

2352
01:28:42,683 --> 01:28:44,853
(I gave it my all.)

2353
01:28:46,523 --> 01:28:50,023
(Welcome, Sister-in-Law)
